{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/912922-recruitment-city-of-fear","id":912922,"title":"Recruitment: City of Fear","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-12T12:20:13-07:00","id":912922,"title":"Recruitment: City of Fear","content":"A series of images:<ul><li>On the 47th floor of a rain-slicked tower of glass, a woman wearing a suit costing more than your rent pushes a novella-sized stack of papers across an onyx-black table in the direction of a group of timid entrepreneurs. It is the terms of their buy-out. They are non-negotiable, if any of them want to leave this room with a cent to their names. Perhaps in the future they will know not to let their reach extend their grasp. The demon lord in the woman's soul smiles contentedly, for dreams have come crashing to the ground today.</li> <li>Waves from a fathomless lake--more sea than pond--batter a cement pier for the thousandth time. Onlookers normally wouldn't bat an eye, but the water's been growing stronger, more directed. On the thousandth-and-first strike, the foundation cracks. It wasn't meant to do that. A population will drown if it's not repaired in time.</li> <li>A cloaked figure is digging up a neglected grave in the back of a city cemetery. It will trade the cadaver it's stealing to a surgeon with too many eyes for the names of proud and fearful individuals who think they can escape death's grasp.</li> <li>In the VIP room of a popular nightclub, a monster cuts open his wrist and bleeds into a mason jar. Another monster takes the blood and mixes it with heroin. A third monster takes that mixture and adds in the juice of a fruit not found anywhere on Earth. A fourth monster will drink this concoction to solidify his hold over the city.</li> <li>In a crumbling, abandoned hotel in one of the most impoverished neighborhoods lies a cube of flesh, the size of a refrigerator. Scattered around it are coins, dolls, needles, and other offerings. The flesh is cool to the touch, but it pulsates slightly. A series of chalk marks on the wall behind the cube record its growth.</li> </ul>I would like to run a game of Beast set in Chicago. It will primarily be character-driven, exploring relationships and the consequences of Hunger, as well as diving into some of the weird things that populate the Windy City. I don't know yet what platform I will run the game on, but for now, if you are interested, post here.<br /> <br /> For the moment, I'm leaving a few things open-ended until I know more about the protagonists of this story. There's a lot of stuff in <i>World of Darkness: Chicago</i> that I like and might repurpose, but I won't necessarily follow everything that's laid out there.<br /> <br /> A few things to lay the groundwork of the setting:<ul><li>Chicago is a city of fears great and small. The poor fear gentrification and city clean-up efforts that push them out of their homes and take away what little they have. The rich fear the grubby masses, heat-packing gangsters, and the urban wilderness. Everyone's at least a little afraid of Lake Michigan, especially when the storms kick up. The Begotten are relatively populous here, and a clever Beast can keep her belly full for a while.</li> <li>Chicago's supernatural landscape is exemplary of the &quot;No neat little boxes&quot; adage. Exploring Kinship can take you to some strange people, places, things, and states of mind. Monstrous politics here are a brutal, tangled web--so complicated and fraught that most Beasts don't even both trying to figure it all out. The Begotten of Chicago have formed Family Ties with sentient trash-heaps, decadent thought-forms, and shapeshifting spider-people.</li> <li>There is a second Chicago in the realm of dreams. The city possesses a strong oneiric reflection that spans the minds of sleepers from O'Hare to Hegewisch. Anyone in the metropolitan area who has a dream about Chicago risks wandering into the nightmare city--and it is indeed a city of nightmares. This mirror is indeed darkly. Skyscrapers loom menacingly, shadows twist into impossible forms, and the torrential rat-swarms in the labyrinthine tunnels will eat anyone who intrudes in their domain alive. Any Chambers made from parts of Chicago can lead into Nightmare Chicago.</li> <li>Prime hunting ground though it may be, powerful Beasts often find their efforts stymied, forced into starvation. Avenues of terror suddenly close up to them, and they find themselves having to lean on Kinships more than usual just to get to normal. Rumors abound about a secret band of heroes, not of the murderous psychopath variety, but a circle dedicated to making the city safer, extraordinary men and women of power and means who are taking on Chicago's fear problems by starving the monsters out of it. A handful of Beasts nearing Inheritance are contemplating rooting out this virtuous band, driving them to desperation, and taking them down in a struggle glorious and terrible. Perhaps the tables have turned a bit too far.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T12:44:21-07:00","id":912940,"title":"","content":"I'm tentatively interested. Have to see how things would be done before I really commit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T18:26:28-07:00","id":913127,"title":"","content":"Maybe...Wondering what I should run.<br /> <br /> EDIT: totes doing a Montauk Monster, so Makara Collector, working out of a museum, collecting downfalls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":1959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","user":"Hexmeister Vic","date":". 06-14-2016, 02:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T07:19:27-07:00","id":914075,"title":"","content":"I'm curious how this game would be played. Are we talking about Roll20 or play by post? If the former, do you know when you are looking to meet up? If the later, have you thought about post minimums and frequency?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5610-aslan751","name":"aslan751","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T09:51:57-07:00","id":914152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aslan751</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/912922-recruitment-city-of-fear?p=914075#post914075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious how this game would be played. Are we talking about Roll20 or play by post? If the former, do you know when you are looking to meet up? If the later, have you thought about post minimums and frequency?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I am leaning more toward a play-by-post style. I hadn't really considered anything like required frequency yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T10:08:21-07:00","id":914165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/912922-recruitment-city-of-fear?p=914152#post914152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think I am leaning more toward a play-by-post style. I hadn't really considered anything like required frequency yet.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd be interested in doing a play-by-post game. Would it be just a Beast game or would it be full-blown crossover? Also, as a side note, it would be remiss to not have a Harry Dresden expy in a CofD Chicago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T10:12:37-07:00","id":914170,"title":"","content":"I would also find play-by-post to be the best option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T14:57:51-07:00","id":914399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/912922-recruitment-city-of-fear?p=914165#post914165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'd be interested in doing a play-by-post game. Would it be just a Beast game or would it be full-blown crossover? Also, as a side note, it would be remiss to not have a Harry Dresden expy in a CofD Chicago.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd like the players to all be Beasts. There can be crossover, you can say &quot;My best friend's a Sin-Eater&quot; or what-have-you, but I'd like all the players to be Begotten. I've never read <i>The Dresden Files</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T20:11:15-07:00","id":914601,"title":"","content":"Alright, good to know. I've already got some character concepts brewing. Wasn't there a CofD Chicago book somewhere?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T20:28:27-07:00","id":914614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/912922-recruitment-city-of-fear?p=914601#post914601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, good to know. I've already got some character concepts brewing. Wasn't there a CofD Chicago book somewhere?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. I love it. I was just looking back over it the other day. Like I mentioned, I might draw inspiration from it, but I don't want anyone to feel bound to what it says about Chicago.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T20:32:34-07:00","id":914616,"title":"","content":"Huh, tentatively interested.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I actually have two Beast concepts, an Ugallu and a Makara. If I'm in, I'll pick one of those.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 06-15-2016, 08:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T20:13:11-07:00","id":915325,"title":"","content":"If it will be a play-by-post, then I would like to say that I am interested as well, provided that posts aren't required at a certain time of day. My work schedule isn't consistent, so committing to anything requiring specific times would be problematic for me, but I would still be capable of getting on to post a bit most days. Is there anything specific that you are looking for as far as the characters go? When would you like to get the characters?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T21:05:41-07:00","id":915365,"title":"","content":"I guess I'll pick based on what the other players have, so there's no overlap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T05:46:33-07:00","id":915539,"title":"","content":"I'm tentatively interested as well. I have a concept but I need to hammer it out a little. I'm thinking Ugallu, probably an Owl.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10415-vermillionde","name":"VermillionDe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T06:13:44-07:00","id":915553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/912922-recruitment-city-of-fear?p=915325#post915325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it will be a play-by-post, then I would like to say that I am interested as well, provided that posts aren't required at a certain time of day. My work schedule isn't consistent, so committing to anything requiring specific times would be problematic for me, but I would still be capable of getting on to post a bit most days. Is there anything specific that you are looking for as far as the characters go? When would you like to get the characters?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I don't think there will be anything as stringent as certain time requirements. I'm leaning toward a post-when-you-can policy, depending on what's going on in a scene.<br /> <br /> I figure we can fully talk characters once I know who's playing and have a posting area set up. In the meantime, here are a few stipulations:<ul><li>You don't have to be a brood if you don't want to. Some can be in a single brood, some might not. You don't have to even like each other, though any starting enmities probably shouldn't be blood feuds quite just yet.</li> <li>Everyone has some connection to someone else. It'll depend on how many players there are, but for now I'm thinking each character has a history of some sort with at least two others. There are wider connections too we'll be mapping out, just to make our ecosystem feel real.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T07:13:20-07:00","id":915580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/912922-recruitment-city-of-fear?p=915553#post915553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, I don't think there will be anything as stringent as certain time requirements. I'm leaning toward a post-when-you-can policy, depending on what's going on in a scene.<br /> <br /> I figure we can fully talk characters once I know who's playing and have a posting area set up. In the meantime, here are a few stipulations:<ul><li>You don't have to be a brood if you don't want to. Some can be in a single brood, some might not. You don't have to even like each other, though any starting enmities probably shouldn't be blood feuds quite just yet.</li> <li>Everyone has some connection to someone else. It'll depend on how many players there are, but for now I'm thinking each character has a history of some sort with at least two others. There are wider connections too we'll be mapping out, just to make our ecosystem feel real.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That makes sense. Characters having encountered each other previously means that there is less effort required to bring the group together. What type of professions would be desirable for characters? Would characters with a basic 9 to 5 job work, or do they require more open schedules? Do you want the characters to be residents of Chicago proper, or would characters who commute in from suburbia work as well? I've got a few ideas forming for characters already, regardless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T07:57:21-07:00","id":915605,"title":"","content":"Hmm... I must say, you have my curiosity, good gentleman.<br /> I may or may not make an application, depending on the technicalities, though a no-settled time PbP does seem like a good enough option, accomodating for many a person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","name":"Inquisitor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T08:33:46-07:00","id":915626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/912922-recruitment-city-of-fear?p=915580#post915580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That makes sense. Characters having encountered each other previously means that there is less effort required to bring the group together. What type of professions would be desirable for characters? Would characters with a basic 9 to 5 job work, or do they require more open schedules? Do you want the characters to be residents of Chicago proper, or would characters who commute in from suburbia work as well? I've got a few ideas forming for characters already, regardless.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think any of those could be interesting situations for a Beast to explore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T08:43:29-07:00","id":915630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/912922-recruitment-city-of-fear?p=915626#post915626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think any of those could be interesting situations for a Beast to explore.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Cool, I'm fairly certain I'm going to be a professor at a local university if that helps anyone make plans.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> Ugallu, Owl, Nemesis for Fraud (exposing frauds). Feeds frequently due to kids cheating in his notoriously difficult behavior and neurology classes, but will often have a project he's working on at the same time, refuting a published work full of holes or looking into the private dealings of city officials. Planning on taking a library as my lair (possibly it's heart). <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10415,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10415-vermillionde","user":"VermillionDe","date":".  Adding in more character details 06-16-2016, 01:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10415-vermillionde","name":"VermillionDe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T08:52:54-07:00","id":915635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VermillionDe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/912922-recruitment-city-of-fear?p=915630#post915630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Cool, I'm fairly certain I'm going to be a professor at a local university if that helps anyone make plans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Artifact Procurer/Museum Preservation Tech at the Field Museum. Character's built, but my computer dislikes interactive character sheets, so I'll move to a different machine to post a link.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T09:28:21-07:00","id":915653,"title":"","content":"I've considered working on either a police detective, a book store owner, or a preacher, if that helps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3514,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","user":"ZealousChristian24","date":". 06-16-2016, 12:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T15:56:25-07:00","id":915896,"title":"","content":"I've got the basic outline of my character down.<br /> <br /> They're either a Collector or a Tyrant, possibly both depending on how you spin it. Whatever I end up deciding on, I've decided that this Beast hungers for vulnerabilities and deeply personal secrets- either to exploit them later (Tyrant) or simply for the delicious knowledge of a secret only <i>they </i>know in addition to that of another (Collector). This Beast uses the secrets and vulnerabilities for the other- enjoying the delicious Satiety and using them as leverage in equal measure.<br /> <br /> For their day job, they either run an occult bookshop and act as a sort of information broker to the supernatural communities of Chicago, as well as a reasonable supplier of potential Ban or Bane materials. They also will accept secrets or lore instead of money as payment, so they tend to know everyone's personal Bans, Banes, Frailties, etc. Alternatively they are a clinical therapist- keeping the Horror reasonably well fed and guiding their now rather alien psychology with the ethics of a therapist.<br /> <br /> The Horror is probably going to be a dragon of some kind, but I'm thinking of maybe going for something a little more eldritch- not quite sure yet. Family is either Eshmaki (Sudden betrayal through secret vulnerabilities) or Ugallu (You can't hide anything from them).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T16:10:41-07:00","id":915903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/912922-recruitment-city-of-fear?p=915896#post915896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've got the basic outline of my character down.<br /> <br /> They're either a Collector or a Tyrant, possibly both depending on how you spin it. Whatever I end up deciding on, I've decided that this Beast hungers for vulnerabilities and deeply personal secrets- either to exploit them later (Tyrant) or simply for the delicious knowledge of a secret only <i>they </i>know in addition to that of another (Collector). This Beast uses the secrets and vulnerabilities for the other- enjoying the delicious Satiety and using them as leverage in equal measure.<br /> <br /> For their day job, they either run an occult bookshop and act as a sort of information broker to the supernatural communities of Chicago, as well as a reasonable supplier of potential Ban or Bane materials. They also will accept secrets or lore instead of money as payment, so they tend to know everyone's personal Bans, Banes, Frailties, etc. Alternatively they are a clinical therapist- keeping the Horror reasonably well fed and guiding their now rather alien psychology with the ethics of a therapist.<br /> <br /> The Horror is probably going to be a dragon of some kind, but I'm thinking of maybe going for something a little more eldritch- not quite sure yet. Family is either Eshmaki (Sudden betrayal through secret vulnerabilities) or Ugallu (You can't hide anything from them).</div> </div> </div> </div>IC, We should do lunch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T16:52:43-07:00","id":915922,"title":"","content":"Kinda cerebral group, I think we'll actually have a lot in common. I'm thinking Geist for family ties. I want access to the underworld, if I don't make my library my heart I'm actually thinking of taking an underworld realm as one of my chambers (library that burned down)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10415-vermillionde","name":"VermillionDe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T18:53:57-07:00","id":915963,"title":"","content":"Since we seem to be expanding on ideas:<br /> <br /> \u2022A Anakim (though I admit he might edge over into Ugallu a little) Nemesis who works as a police detective and whose Horror manifests as a Talos-style giant with red and blue searchlights for eyes, representing the inevitability of law. He may be Wolfblooded, and either way he has some strong connections with the Lodge of the Shield. I'm thinking he's going to be making positive inroads with Kin or supernatural groups focused on upholding the law... though I imagine he struggles with how far is too far with going outside the law to enforce it.<br /> <br /> \u2022A Namtaru Nemesis that serves as a preacher and whose Horror takes the shape of an oversized preying mantis with vaguely humanesque features, who is meant to represent the fear of being the reason for one's own failures. He seeks to scare the wicked into the arms of God, which would put him on good terms with the Lancea Sanctum if he didn't despise everything they stand for. Not only do they speak what he sees as heresy, they claim that vampires are innately Dammed, which clashes with the core of his philosophy, in which he believed that anyone can strive to be good, and that any supernatural strangeness is just another issue to be overcome. Sees himself as a very &quot;tough love&quot; sort of teacher. Likely going to develop (contentious) links to other Kin interested in the immortal souls of themselves and mortals. <br /> <br /> \u2022A Makara Collector as encapsulated <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/541856-beast-character-idea-thread?p=898111#post898111\">here</a>, a cunning sea serpent who takes a keen interest in the sorceries of his Kin and has some serious envy issues. The sister would come into play later, I imagine; mostly I'd start by having him develop inroads with other supernaturals to feed his hunger for objects of ocult power and lore and to live though the spells of others. I imagined he'd run a bookstore or something; if I go with this one, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1959_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1959\" data-vbnamecard=\"1959\">Hexmeister Vic</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4152\" data-vbnamecard=\"4152\">Arcanist</a>, <i>all</i> of them might have to do lunch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T21:03:56-07:00","id":916020,"title":"","content":"I am almost dead sure that my character will be a therapist- there's just too many plot hooks there not to take advantage of, and the Beast can feed basically guilt-free. Getting a patient to confide in you is necessary to be a good therapist. Of course, if this guy goes off the rails, he could be really horrific. Like, Hannibal Lecter horrific. Plus it gives him this code he can really strive to uphold. Kinship is almost certainly with Changelings- I can see him serving as a Freehold shrink. Might even have a Lair Chamber in the Hedge. Considering how cerebral, social, and well fed this character will probably end up being, I think they'll likely end up specializing in Nightmares.<br /> <br /> Only question is, what should I do for my starting Atavisms? There's just too many great ones, and more or less all of them fit for a dragon.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3514\" data-vbnamecard=\"3514\">ZealousChristian24</a> I really like that Makara Collector idea. It's such a juicy character. And Mage 2e is out, so there won't be any edition clashes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 06-17-2016, 12:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T21:08:41-07:00","id":916022,"title":"","content":"These are really good ideas. I'm liking them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T05:33:33-07:00","id":916137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/912922-recruitment-city-of-fear?p=916020#post916020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only question is, what should I do for my starting Atavisms? There's just too many great ones, and more or less all of them fit for a dragon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, depending on whether you're going to be an Eshmaki or Ugallu will influence that decision I imagine, since you have to take one of their starting. I suppose you could choose thematically based on how you'll use the information (whether you'll hide it until you surprise your target with it, or whether you'll rain it down on them) or you could decide which Atavisms you absolutely need to start the game, and then see if one of them is Ugallu or Eshmaki. <br /> <br /> I know a Dragon can be an Eshmaki, but I feel like thematically that's not usually the case. I mean, with Eshmaki I feel like you aren't supposed to see them until the moment of the kill, legends about Dragons usually show them in all of their terrifying glory first. Unless they're wingless, I can see them being pretty well defined as Ugallu. That is however highly motivated by personal opinion, I know that a Dragon could realistically fit into any of the families. <br /> <br /> Personally I'm planning on doing Storm Lashed and Mimir's Wisdom as my starting Atavisms, if that helps. I have a WIP character sheet, I'll post a (probably low quality) image of it later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10415-vermillionde","name":"VermillionDe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T06:38:50-07:00","id":916153,"title":"","content":"I have a few characters in mind, but the one that seems to be developing the most quickly is an EPA water quality compliance enforcer that travels around the Chicagoland area testing the water at various facilities as part of his 9 to 5 job. He would most likely be a Namtaru Nemesis that preyed on people who polluted the environment, especially the water. His job would allow him plenty of opportunity for low level feedings, although he'd need to get a bit more creative in order to feed at higher levels of Satiety. The Horror would be a dragon frog, and the lair would be a polluted swamp. This is still fairly rough, of course, and may yet change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T07:02:15-07:00","id":916164,"title":"","content":"Well, since everyone seems to be throwing down their character concepts, I'm gonna do this too.<br /> So the base premise is an Ugallu(Or Anakim, I have not decided yet) Ravager, a former military fighter pilot (Discharged after a crippling injury he suffered after being shot down by a surface-to-air missle), currently working as a security advisor. His horror manifests as a vaguely draconic beast, flying above in the sky of the lair and gunning down unfortunate dream visitors with precisely aimed fireballs. Pretty much embodying the fears of victims of drone warfare, though I'm not completely set on his way of feeding yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","name":"Inquisitor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T08:26:17-07:00","id":916227,"title":"","content":"Huh- what is it about Beast and an inclination to play dragons? Is it just that they're such prevelant and charismatic monsters? That being said, I am totally okay with playing a Brood full of dragons.<br /> <br /> The therapist day job makes me inclined to think Ugallu. He's the guy you can't hide anything from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T09:13:11-07:00","id":916256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/912922-recruitment-city-of-fear?p=916227#post916227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh- what is it about Beast and an inclination to play dragons? Is it just that they're such prevelant and charismatic monsters? That being said, I am totally okay with playing a Brood full of dragons.<br /> <br /> The therapist day job makes me inclined to think Ugallu. He's the guy you can't hide anything from.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not <i>all </i>Dragons. Some of us are benighted creatures from the space between the stars<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T09:14:56-07:00","id":916258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/912922-recruitment-city-of-fear?p=916227#post916227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh- what is it about Beast and an inclination to play dragons? Is it just that they're such prevelant and charismatic monsters? That being said, I am totally okay with playing a Brood full of dragons.<br /> <br /> The therapist day job makes me inclined to think Ugallu. He's the guy you can't hide anything from.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the game had originally been pitched as a dragon game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> One of the bright side to dragons is that they are easily recognizable creatures despite the fact that they have an incredible degree of variation in appearance. My character's Horror seems like what you might end up with if a frog or a toad mated with a dragon. It's appearance would mostly be that of a giant amphibian, but with vestigial wings and a mouth full of sharp fangs.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Of course, if too many dragons seems to be a problem, I could always work on the magician with the monster rabbit Horror...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","user":"White Oak Dragon","date":".  added the alternate character concept 06-17-2016, 12:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T09:44:03-07:00","id":916278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/912922-recruitment-city-of-fear?p=916258#post916258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: Of course, if too many dragons seems to be a problem, I could always work on the magician with the monster rabbit Horror...</div> </div> </div> </div>I &lt;3 this idea<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10415-vermillionde","name":"VermillionDe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T13:33:13-07:00","id":916398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/912922-recruitment-city-of-fear?p=916258#post916258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> EDIT: Of course, if too many dragons seems to be a problem, I could always work on the magician with the monster rabbit Horror...</div> </div> </div> </div>This is both crazy, awesome and ridiculous. What fear would this guy actually be though?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","name":"Inquisitor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T14:43:20-07:00","id":916440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Inquisitor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/912922-recruitment-city-of-fear?p=916398#post916398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is both crazy, awesome and ridiculous. What fear would this guy actually be though?</div> </div> </div> </div> As an Eshmaki it might represent a fear of trickery, of the terror that comes when you know someone's deceiving you but don't understand their true aim or mechanism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T15:01:48-07:00","id":916447,"title":"","content":"I could also see a namtaru, taking something safe and turning it vicious. Loss of innocence and all that, kinda like what psychonauts did with the meat circus","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10415-vermillionde","name":"VermillionDe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T16:20:18-07:00","id":916475,"title":"","content":"The loss of innocence sums it up pretty well. The magician would desire to bring wonder into the world, and to prevent the innocence of others from being torn away. While he would acknowledge that a certain amount of innocence being lost is a part of growing up, he would see a distinct difference between losing it &quot;properly&quot; and having it brutally ripped away. He will probably be either Eshmaki or Namtaru. Hunger is a bit trickier, as a lot of them could work well. Tyrant, Predator, and Nemesis are the most likely ones that I'll be considering. The bunny monster will most likely end up looking something like a wolpertinger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T19:48:57-07:00","id":916566,"title":"","content":"If you still have space and I end up playing, I'd be either a Mothwoman or a Kraken, so no worries about dragon overload.<br /> <br /> More specifically, the concepts I'd choose between are &quot;conspiracy theorist detective whose Horror is a giant moth&quot; and &quot;crooked businesswoman with mafia connections whose Horror is a sea creature resembling the Cloverfield monster with numerous tentacle-like arms&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T03:57:22-07:00","id":916761,"title":"","content":"Alternatively, the magician could be representing the fear of realizing that the world is not the way you think it is(Which I think suits a Makara pretty well, doesn't it?). You know, dogs don't eat cats, rabbits are murderous terryfying stuff of nightmares, that kinda thing.<br /> That, or the fear of too many Monty Python references. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","name":"Inquisitor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T09:31:11-07:00","id":916874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Inquisitor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/912922-recruitment-city-of-fear?p=916761#post916761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alternatively, the magician could be representing the fear of realizing that the world is not the way you think it is(Which I think suits a Makara pretty well, doesn't it?). You know, dogs don't eat cats, rabbits are murderous terryfying stuff of nightmares, that kinda thing.<br /> That, or the fear of too many Monty Python references. :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes! That is exactly it! The nasty, big pointy teeth adorning the face of a creature that is usually seen as harmless and innocent come as a rude shock to anyone that thinks that world works in an easily understood manner. Anybody who thinks that they know what's going on is going to be shocked to discover that this rabbit's got a vicious streak a mile wide. I think that the character will probably be Eshmaki, giving the darkness's ability to conceal the truth of the world and the Horror's ability to reveal just what kind of terrors lurk within it. The character ultimately wants to remove the blinders that people put on. He wants people to look at a world full of endless possibilities. Ideally, they get to that state in a manner that promotes a love of exploration and a desire to find new discoveries. Of course, some people are a bit harder to accomplish that with than others. Some people too easily dismiss a sound as &quot;just the wind&quot; without further thought. These ones might need something a bit more obvious. Wide-eyed wonder is what he wants, but if it takes a bit of bone chilling fear in order to open their eyes, then he might just need to go that route.<br /> <br /> I am still trying to decide on his Hunger, though. I could see him as a Tyrant, taking nourishment from the moment that the target realizes that there is more going on than realized. The character would be able to feed by forcing a target to accept a new view of the world. As a Predator, he'd be feeding on those little lines that a person draws between what is and what isn't possible, taking a little of each target's boundaries of belief. The character might be able to feed lightly by truly mystifying an audience (an easier feat if there a lot of children present), but deeper feedings might require driving a skeptic to tears with fear of occult forces that are becoming undeniable. If he was a Nemesis, he would be punishing those that destroy the innocence or sense of wonder in others. He would take an especially dim view of those that did harm to children. All of these traits are ones that I'm seeing for the character, although I'm leaning more towards the Tyrant or the Predator.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T13:47:31-07:00","id":916973,"title":"","content":"So this is the writeup I went with. Professional Training Skills are Empathy, Persuasion, and Medicine. <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_VOpIH9hXNwNVRtZlFodnM5U0E/view\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_V...FodnM5U0E/view</a><br /> <br /> I'm still thinking of a name for the character and the Horror, but I'm rather happy with how the character turned out. They're a lot more social-oriented than I thought they would be, but Dragonfire still packs a kick, and in the Lair it would be even more potent. The Lair has two Chambers, the Heart and a Chamber based off of the local Hedge, and as such is filled with thorny underbrush, and thick, ever-shifting forests. The Heart is in a clearing, with strange menhirs carved with eldritch symbols. Hanging from the menhirs and the tallest trees are scraps of parchment and symbolic items bundled together, looking like some combination of effigy and fetish, representing people whose weaknesses the Beast ferreted out and collected. Some are stained with dried blood, from those who the Beast killed when they had no other choice. The Horror is a dragon, long and slender, resembling a Perentie in shape but with the blunted face, gorgeous coloration, and heavily keeled scales of Atheris Hispida. The creature's hide is a burnished yellow-gold, with black accents throughout and a paler underside, with extremely alert and intelligent silver eyes. The claws are surprisingly delicate, and the long crescent-shaped wings on its back are not yet strong enough to hold it aloft. The skin is warm and pliant to the touch between the keels.<br /> <br /> The Beast had always been interested in dreams and their purpose to the human mind- they didn't serve the same sort of purpose instincts did. He followed his pursuit for truth, and his fascination with repeating global symbols, like the solar cross and the dragon, into university, where he began studying to become a psychiatrist in an effort to understand the human condition and, therefore, to understand himself. He was blind to his own failings, until the Devouring, and now he tries to teach the lesson that you must acknowledge your weaknesses to overcome them. Though the Horror within cares not a whit about human life, and would indeed prefer to consume victims through exploiting their weaknesses, the Beast chains himself to a rigid ethical code- that of a clinical therapist. He seeks to teach the lesson through <i>healing </i>pain, not inflicting it, in an effort to overcome and transcend even the Horror's shortcomings.<br /> <br /> In pursuit of the nature of dreams, the Beast came across the Lost and made a name for himself as a specialist in occult trauma, encouraging them to face their traumas head-on and accept them so that they may attempt to master them. This is a suitable arrangement for everyone involved, as the Beast is equally well-versed in the nature of dreams as the Lost, is extremely accepting and non-judgemental, and even shares a good deal of himself with them. His therapy sessions are always intimate and cathartic, and it is the catharsis that he pursues, because it is the shock of acknowledging and accepting trauma- the experience of which is freely shared with him -that keeps the Horror well-fed. The Beast wishes to expand his relationship with the Freehold, becoming an official Oathbound member and their official psychiatrist. Post-Devouring, the Beast has become a lot more spiritual than he had been before (being a living nightmare from the collective human soul will do that) and is more than a little obsessed with continuing to discover the true nature of dreams; he wishes to track down a much older dragon to learn at their feet, and even find some evidence that the Dark Mother is a literal, physical reality. He has so much he wants to ask her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T15:32:10-07:00","id":917011,"title":"","content":"Awesome character, Arcanist. The visuals on the character are especially interesting. I'd never heard of either of those reptiles before, and the two images combined makes for a spectacular dragon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T18:19:02-07:00","id":917072,"title":"","content":"Are there still openings? I'm very interested.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5610-aslan751","name":"aslan751","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T19:39:25-07:00","id":917105,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4152\" data-vbnamecard=\"4152\">Arcanist</a> That's an intriguing concept. I see you've already determined your starting Satiety. Care to break that down for me? <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5610-aslan751\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5610_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5610\" data-vbnamecard=\"5610\">aslan751</a> Maybe? Could I get a show of hands of who is on board now? I feel like I could handle a max of five players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T20:00:17-07:00","id":917114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/912922-recruitment-city-of-fear?p=917105#post917105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4152\" data-vbnamecard=\"4152\">Arcanist</a> That's an intriguing concept. I see you've already determined your starting Satiety. Care to break that down for me?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5610-aslan751\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5610_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5610\" data-vbnamecard=\"5610\">aslan751</a> Maybe? Could I get a show of hands of who is on board now? I feel like I could handle a max of five players.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm in, just need to finish up my backstory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T20:08:51-07:00","id":917117,"title":"","content":"I'm in as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T20:18:02-07:00","id":917124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/912922-recruitment-city-of-fear?p=917105#post917105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4152\" data-vbnamecard=\"4152\">Arcanist</a> That's an intriguing concept. I see you've already determined your starting Satiety. Care to break that down for me?</div> </div> </div> </div>Certainly. A Beast character starts with Satiety 2. I have non-Beast Kin (Changelings) so that adds a point. My character feeds easily, so that adds another. He doesn't hunt with other Begotten, and he likes showing off his true self, so he doesn't get additional Satiety from that. And he starts with only Lair 1, so another point of Satiety. Satiety 2 + 3 = Satiety 5.<br /> <br /> I am so very ready for this game- if only I had a name for my character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T20:18:15-07:00","id":917125,"title":"","content":"I'll take a spot if i can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5610-aslan751","name":"aslan751","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T21:18:17-07:00","id":917155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/912922-recruitment-city-of-fear?p=917124#post917124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am so very ready for this game- if only I had a name for my character.</div> </div> </div> </div>How about Beastie McBeastalot? If you're actually looking for assistance coming up with a name, I can also give serious suggestions. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T21:48:40-07:00","id":917175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/912922-recruitment-city-of-fear?p=917105#post917105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Could I get a show of hands of who is on board now? I feel like I could handle a max of five players.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm in as well. I have a character sheet done. I'll posy my synopsis here in a few. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10415-vermillionde","name":"VermillionDe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T22:06:39-07:00","id":917180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B6ZjaASU2ixbanRIUzd6TU5KZ1E/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B6ZjaASU2ixbanRIUzd6TU5KZ1E/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B6ZjaASU2ixbanRIUzd6TU5KZ1E/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B6ZjaASU2ixbanRIUzd6TU5KZ1E/view?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I'm thinking for the concept of the character that as a child (and up until his becoming) that he had constant nightmares about finding a book that was missing. He'd run from crooked shelf to shelf looking among the ashes of burnt parchment remains as the dread grew stronger. In truth what he felt was that the Beast in him had been damaged horribly in a previous incarnation and many of the books he held dear were lost. However, the Horror knew that not all that is destroyed is gone. Sometimes things slip between the cracks, falling into other realms. That the underworld holds many a lost library to time.<br /> <br /> The Horror takes the shape of a giant owl, twice as tall as a man. Thin in proportion with exaggerated beak and talons but nothing can detract from it's enormous, wide yellow eyes, unblinking and unwavering. It's coloring brown and black in patterns that almost appear like a lost script. Omen knows that the pursuit of truth is not just the most enviable quest, it is the only one. As such those who would fabricate bring us all low and must pay a terrible price for their crimes.<br /> <br /> The heart of Omen's lair is a great tree, forming a maze of many intertwining root systems. Each root has wrought into it shelves holding books, parchments, carvings and ancient forgotten languages. Or many did, before the hunter came. Now the frigid heights of the tree contain burnt limbs and ashen shelves. The ravens that carried the books and scrolls to their shelves now sound their mourning in cacophony and pick through delicate ash heaps, looking for the scraps that remain. While the books may be gone, the memories of what was read remains, it is enough until copies can be recovered. Already in a several blind forays into the underworld has a destroyed library been found, taking up a vacant chamber in the lair. However without a guide the underworld is a treacherous place. Clearly, more study is required.<br /> <br /> Samuel Albertine was always an odd child. Born to a family with means and high expectations, he was noteworthy for a lack of interest in the people around him. However the dusty library his father kept was full of worlds he could almost touch, and somehow were already familiar to him. The round rimless glasses that sat low on his nose were constantly reflecting in the dim light. In an effort to force the young child into a semblance of social interaction, Samuel's parents forced him to take up a sport of some kind. Rather than doing something brutish and competitive, he decided track and gymnastics were a sport of form and technique. His coach used to say that he spent more time with his feet off the ground than on it.<br /> <br /> Getting into the professional world was another matter. Samuel felt constant dread that he didn't know ENOUGH to be good at what he did, did he really belong where he was? Could he teach what he knew to others? Was he SURE he was good enough at what he knew? After he discovered the true nature of what he was those feelings calmed. The answers were waiting, and like anything else in his life it was just a matter of finding the right book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10415,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10415-vermillionde","user":"VermillionDe","date":". 06-19-2016, 01:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10415-vermillionde","name":"VermillionDe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T02:30:18-07:00","id":917257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/912922-recruitment-city-of-fear?p=917105#post917105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe? Could I get a show of hands of who is on board now? I feel like I could handle a max of five players.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, I'm on alright. Character's dropping by later today.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","name":"Inquisitor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T06:45:07-07:00","id":917318,"title":"","content":"Aaand here's the character sheet: <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/8q4y6zxneo8776f/Elias.pdf?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.dropbox.com/s/8q4y6zxneo...Elias.pdf?dl=0</a> Asset skills are Drive, Firearms and Survival.<br /> Also a question to the Storyteller, regarding nightmares and determinig satiety: Would Cheiron Group Hunters be elligible for kinship, with all their taumatechnology implantations and whatnot?<br /> Aaand here's his backstory and fluff.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Elias' story started off as many before him and many after him. Expanding upon his childhood fascination with airplanes, he chased the career of a pilot. Of course, shortly after he entered the adult life, the country got involved in another sensless war for oil, and, due to a combination of idealistic idiocy and thrill-seeking he decided to become a fighter pilot. After a couple years duing which he completed all the required trainings, passed the required exams and whatnot, he became an active pilot in service of the US Air Force, and was promply sent somewhere where he could be useful, namely Iraq.<br /> There, Elias realized two things. First is that he wasn't quite fighting the good fight for the truth, justice and democracy, which wasn't that much of a surprise. Second was that all the death and destruction he was dealing from up high, every missle he fired, every life he took, every smoldering wreckage he left behind on a successfull mission, it filled him with some weird feeling. Feeling of accomplishment, of joy, of satisfaction. He figured out that he liked what he was doing, all the destruction and ruin. At one of his missions, however, a lucky MANPAD missle put this to stop. His jet got hit. Elias promptly lost control over the handicapped vehicle and crashed. He crawled out of the wreckage, heavily wounded, and promptly tried to somehow bring himself to relative working order, before losing conciousness.<br /> While unconcious, he was visited by a dream. The same one that haunted him regularily from the very beginning of his career. He was standing there, in the middle of a scorched desert, earth marked with cracks and craters, with a couple weak looking cases of growth a generous person might describe as plants, stretching as far as eye can see and then some. On the horizon, a visage of some sort of city, or a village. In the sky, an indiscernible winged silhouette, flying around, the slow, quiet swooshes of it's wings repearing regularily, still drumming in the back of the consciousness. And when Elias decided to make way to the city, the offensive began. The silhouette dived down quickly, firing a couple balls of fire at Elias, all of them missing their mark, but still hitting the earth around him with thunderous force, enough to knock him down. Nevertheless, he continued his walk, and the firing repeated itself a couple times, fountains of earth, rocks and gravel firing from the ground at Elias, bruising and cutting him, but not injuring much. Persistent, he arrvied at the city. A disorganized mass of clay cottages and houses, small or big box-like creations, stacked with one another, narrow streets making ways between them. But he knew that they wouldn't shelter him. The blasts of fire wrecked every house he entered, or tried to, large pieces of clay flying around, hitting him more often than not. Finally, after a couple eternities of such situation, his injuries now exactly replicating those he suffered in the crash, he managed to get himself to a place where he could no longer run from. Cornered at the roof of the tallest building, he expected one last blast to finish him off. But instead, the enormous draconic creature in the sky descended and stood before him on the roof and looked down on him curiously. Elias started to laugh. And then the beast ate him.<br /> He awoke in an infirmary, apparently connected to all sorts of medical apparatus and shortly after a surgery. From the information he managed to gather, he was spotted and recovered by a nearby patrol, shortly after falling unconcious. They managed to secure him just enough that he could be transported to a place where he could hopefully be taken better care of. And, miraculously, his life was indeed saved. What wasn't saved, however, was his humanity. Beacause from that moment on, Elias was a Beast.<br /> Shortly after he managed to recover, due to the fact that in the crash he managed to lose an eye(Said eye is now cyclically being regenerated by a certain Thyrsus mage, in exchange for various favours.), Elias was discharged from the military and moved to Chicago, where he got involved in the local supernatural community.<br /> <br /> How does his situation look at the current point in time?<br /> Currently Elias has managed to deeply lodge himself in position as the leader of a Hunter Cell including members of the Union and the Cheiron Group. The members of the cell think it's just a usual hunter cell... Well, as usual as a Cheiron/Union mixed cell can be, although amongst some more aware parts of the city's Hunter community, especially the Lucifuge, they have a reputation of notoriously commiting so called &quot;<a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/VanHelsingHateCrimes\" target=\"_blank\">Van Helsing Hate Crimes</a>&quot;. None of them however know of the fact that the cell is a cancer cell, and it's better for it to stay this way.<br /> The truth about the cell, known in the supernatural community, is that they serve as a mercenary hit squad, directed by Elias at whatever target his client wants taken care of, in exchange for various items or services, ranging from a &quot;dinner invitation&quot; to various items of power. About the only group that hasn't in the passing years used their services even once is the organized Demon agencies. Elias also deals other than assassinations, including using his current job as a security advisor for a couple of companies to leave a couple holes in their systems and then selling information about them to willing buyers.<br /> <br /> The horror that places itself where Elias' soul used to be manifests itself as a sizable wyvern, of a deep red, almost black coloration, surprisingly reminescent of the armadillo grilled lizard fused with an unidentifiable carnosaurus, with a short, rather barrel-shaped body, massive muscular pillar-like legs similiar to those of modern day ostriches, a thick heavy tail, helping it keep balance , and an elongated head adorned with many curious horns and spikes, forming a crest in the back, as well as some pyramid-shaped smaller spikes more towards the front and a pair of whiskers similiar to those of a catfish. Most of it's body is covered in plate-like scales, forming more spikes along it's body, but being surprisingly soft to touch, offering barely any protection from attacks. In adition, spikes running along it's spine can open itself up to reveal a sail crest, for reasons unknown. The creature utilizes it's enormous wings in a manner similiar to pterosaurs, using them as help when walking.<br /> <br /> The Lair is divided into two chambers. The first one, that also serves as it's heart is the one described in the third paragraph. The second one is based the military base Elias resided in before coming back to the States from Iraq. A great area covered by excersise squares, landing pads, parking areas and whatnot, with a couple hangars, barrracks, garages and other buildings scattered around the place. All around, air sirens are ringing out, signalizing an aerial attack incoming. People around (If the good Storyteller accepts the idea of dream extras in the lair, if not, scratch that, the base is empty) are running frantically, trying to escape or mount some sort of defence, but the gates are locked down and the fences seem to be stretched out miles high upwards. Looking upwards, the wyvern's silhouette is painted upon the sky, roaring of it's wings bearly hearable... And when the visitor to the lair realizes that, the wyvern begins it's bombardment.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Jeesus, that came out waaay too long. Does anyone here have anything against what was written down above?<br /> EDIT: Alongside the changes in the character sheet, a starting satiety breakdown:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Who are your kin? Elias has, to a degree, bonded with the Cheiron Group employees in his Cell. It's not much of the traditional Beast-other supernaturals Big Brother-Little Brother relationship, but more of a &quot;Father to His Men&quot; kind of thing. They are his squad, and while it may not seem like much, for Elias it's kind of a big deal.<br /> Does your belly fill easily? No. Elias' feedings are to a degree associated with the hits and hunts his cell undertakes, which are oftentimes irregular, happening in larger intervals and usually taking up a lot of planning.<br /> Are you a social predator? Nope. Elias generally doesn't hold that big of an opinion on other children. The whole &quot;Lessons&quot; thing they have going on reminds him a lot of the Middle East.<br /> How frequently do you show your true self? Not often, really. He has to keep a low profile to not gain the KOS status amongst his men.<br /> How drawn to your Lair are you? Barely. Elias and the Wyvern are as much conflicted as it is possible for them to be, really.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11117,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","user":"Inquisitor","date":". 06-20-2016, 12:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","name":"Inquisitor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T08:12:24-07:00","id":917360,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11117_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11117\" data-vbnamecard=\"11117\">Inquisitor</a> That's quite the backstory. I like it. I'm seeing some things that eventually I'd like to hear you expound on. Your Dropbox link appears to be broken. Regarding Cheiron hunters: I think they can count if you'd like. Is there like a custom Kinship Nightmare you were thinking of?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10415-vermillionde\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10415\" data-vbnamecard=\"10415\">VermillionDe</a> Nice backstory as well. The book thing is cool, especially the connection to the Underworld. I think you need to change the permissions on your Google Doc; I can't currently access it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T09:17:38-07:00","id":917387,"title":"","content":"Well done on your characters, VermillionDe and Inquisitor! Both of those are wonderful descriptions and backstories.<br /> <br /> I'm working on my character sheet now, although I won't get a chance to finish it until tonight after work or tomorrow morning. I was wondering, though, whether we are limited to the 10 archetypes listed in the book for Legend and Life, or if we were free to create our own?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission State