":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10415-vermillionde","name":"VermillionDe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T17:38:22-07:00","id":917656,"title":"","content":"Is there any more room in the open call? Been wanting to try a hand a being a PC in a Beast Chronicle for a while, and absolutely adore what's been written so far. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T17:52:27-07:00","id":917663,"title":"","content":"I'm afraid it's all full up now. Sorry!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T18:05:15-07:00","id":917678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VermillionDe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/912922-recruitment-city-of-fear?p=917655#post917655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@<b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic\">Hexmeister Vic</a></b>, any chance your research on this mummy (or another project) would require an MRI? If that's the case we may have met if you needed to use equipment from the university.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably. Good idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T19:27:03-07:00","id":917726,"title":"","content":"Ah, worth a shot anyway. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T21:22:18-07:00","id":917779,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10415-vermillionde\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10415\" data-vbnamecard=\"10415\">VermillionDe</a> Our characters almost definitely know each other- I could see my character being a guest lecturer in one of your character's classes. You know, I imagine Beasts are big followers of Jung, considering that they have first-hand experience supporting his beliefs. They're also likely interested in Campbell, and likely rather critical. Would we share a Brood Lair? I can see these two associating pretty closely, and mine being extremely eager to help him fill in that library in order to help fulfill his own agenda.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar309_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"309\" data-vbnamecard=\"309\">White Oak Dragon</a> That makes sense. In which case he probably hasn't seen your character in at least two years- he's a real stickler for the ethics of psychotherapy, and that entails no professional contact for a while in order to avoid potentially compromising recovery with multiple relationships. I can imagine that my character tried to be a mentor to the younger Begotten early on.<br /> <br /> Oh, and I came up with a name for my character. Dorian Long. The Changelings know him as Dr. Thorn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T06:09:25-07:00","id":917978,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4152\" data-vbnamecard=\"4152\">Arcanist</a>, I'm cool with sharing a lair on two conditions: One, I don't want to be a part of the larger Hive. I'm cool with sharing it with another Beast(s) as long as I know who they are, I just don't want unknown people in there. Two, any guests are either escorted or I get informed of them (which is something I would reciprocate with). Omen (my horror) is going to be EXTREMELY sensitive about people in his lair after what happened to him. Otherwise, yeah I'd be happy to share a brood lair. I imagine our characters would be pretty like minded. Of course we probably spend just as much time arguing as agreeing. <br /> <br /> Speaking of: Yes, it'd be hard to deny Jung or Campbell's work given the Primordial dream, as well as access to the Tenemos and any individual Oneiros. Granted, a lot like Freud's early work it'd be looked at as an admirable first attempt with some understandable misses in accuracy. Particularly because Jung never considered that a collective unconscious might be a predatory ingress for humanity rather than a source of collected information. It would lend to a different perspective on a number of mental illnesses who's sources might actually be from having too much or too little contact with said collective unconscious.<br /> <br /> Additionally, given my character's perspective as a Neurologist first and psychologist second, he would be very much interested in studying the physical pathways in the brain that may lead to access to the primordial dream and if those connections could be altered, enhanced or even severed (and anyone who is a beast and has met him should expect to have been asked repeatedly if they'd be willing to let me take an EEG of them). I probably hold a (unpopular) belief that Heroes are functionally similar to schizophrenic individuals who receive too much stimulation from those pathways and seek to purge the &quot;noisiest&quot; sources. Granted, after what happened to him he's unlikely to equate that theory with any kind of sympathy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10415-vermillionde","name":"VermillionDe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T07:23:53-07:00","id":918021,"title":"","content":"I'm sure Dorian would be perfectly fine with that. He isn't exactly starving and he doesn't see his food supply drying up anytime soon. A vitriolic friendship with undercurrents of mutual pursuit of ambitions suits me just fine- lots of fuel for stories there.<br /> <br /> Yeah, we'll be looking at the nature of dreams, the mind, and the soul a lot, I think. Changeling spoilers even imply that dreams are what allow people to replenish their Willpower with rest, either through contact with the collective soul of humanity, or contact with their own Daimon in the Oneiros (I'm going to go with Temenos-contact though. The symbolism filters down from there, and the Soulless don't replenish Willpower from rest). It then suggests interesting things about the Hedge and Arcadia, especially since Changelings vanish into the Hedge when they sleep if they choose to dream. We're going to be mad scientists, academic philosophers, and sage occultists. This is going to be great.<br /> <br /> What I think Dorian would really like to do is hook up an EEG to a Beast communing with the Horror without actually entering the Lair- then they could see which pathways the Horror operates at.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T07:40:10-07:00","id":918028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/912922-recruitment-city-of-fear?p=918021#post918021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changeling spoilers even imply that dreams are what allow people to replenish their Willpower with rest, either through contact with the collective soul of humanity, or contact with their own Daimon in the Oneiros (I'm going to go with Temenos-contact though. The symbolism filters down from there, and the Soulless don't replenish Willpower from rest). It then suggests interesting things about the Hedge and Arcadia, especially since Changelings vanish into the Hedge when they sleep if they choose to dream.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, that's interesting. We might even be able to cross reference some of that information with beings who have a stronger connection to other realms, for instance: do the dead still dream? Geist's have a willpower track but they're functionally dead, so do they still have a connection to the hedge for purposes of dreaming or do they pull the same personal replenishment out of the underworld. ... I feel like we should apologize to @espiritdecalmar in advance for all the crap we're going to be looking into. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/912922-recruitment-city-of-fear?p=918021#post918021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're going to be mad scientists, academic philosophers, and sage occultists. This is going to be great.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know. We're going to be completely intolerable to anyone not from an academic background, it's going to be fantastic. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/912922-recruitment-city-of-fear?p=918021#post918021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> What I think Dorian would really like to do is hook up an EEG to a Beast communing with the Horror without actually entering the Lair- then they could see which pathways the Horror operates at.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was my thinking too, but I want to use a voltimiter before we use an EEG for that. I don't want to have to explain to the university how someone generated enough synaptic activity to fry a 6 figure brain scanning machine. Or how they survived the experience.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10415-vermillionde","name":"VermillionDe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T08:10:36-07:00","id":918045,"title":"","content":"Welp. The inter-character dynamic is shaping up pretty nicely between Dorian and Samuel, at the very least. Many a Magistos will be nagged by those two. I'm personally waiting for all the characters (Hurry up, Oak!) to be up before I start establishing any relations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","name":"Inquisitor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T09:14:12-07:00","id":918066,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11117_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11117\" data-vbnamecard=\"11117\">Inquisitor</a> I can totally see your character falling for letting us examine you once, then never again. Particularly if you let it slip that your eye was being regenerated by other means.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10415-vermillionde","name":"VermillionDe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T09:26:16-07:00","id":918070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VermillionDe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/912922-recruitment-city-of-fear?p=918066#post918066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11117_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11117\" data-vbnamecard=\"11117\">Inquisitor</a> I can totally see your character falling for letting us examine you once, then never again. Particularly if you let it slip that your eye was being regenerated by other means.</div> </div> </div> </div>The whole thing would basically be:<br /> &quot;You want to stick some electrodes to a Beast and see what happens?&quot;<br /> &quot;Pretty much.&quot;<br /> &quot;How much do you pay?&quot;<br /> And a couple days later all your Resources dots are gone and your research hasn't moved one bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","name":"Inquisitor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T09:31:36-07:00","id":918072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Inquisitor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/912922-recruitment-city-of-fear?p=918070#post918070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The whole thing would basically be:<br /> &quot;You want to stick some electrodes to a Beast and see what happens?&quot;<br /> &quot;Pretty much.&quot;<br /> &quot;How much do you pay?&quot;<br /> And a couple days later all your Resources dots are gone and your research hasn't moved one bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pff, you make it sound like that isn't how that normally goes. Besides, Samuel is a certified, decorated academic. He doesn't use his OWN money for studies. The university can fund the research that is totally not about Beasts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10415-vermillionde","name":"VermillionDe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T09:33:05-07:00","id":918073,"title":"","content":"My character would be more interested in the physics of t