":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10415-vermillionde","name":"VermillionDe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T17:14:14-07:00","id":918328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VermillionDe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/912922-recruitment-city-of-fear?p=918324#post918324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar309_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"309\" data-vbnamecard=\"309\">White Oak Dragon</a> Your Lair is super creepy, I like it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks. I'm glad you liked it. I was trying to go for something that was creepy but that would still have the feel of wonderment that the character adores. I haven't yet decided on what the second Chamber will be, or whether I'll just cash it in for 2 Experiences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T17:53:40-07:00","id":918346,"title":"","content":"This is all fantastic stuff. Great job everybody!<br /> <br /> Okay, so tomorrow I'm taking a trip out of state for a week, so I won't be able to reply much. However, I have a bunch of questions for you guys to ponder and answer in the meantime. Next week, I'll set up where we'll be playing, figure out what other beginning questions need to be addressed, and then hopefully we'll dive right in glub glub glub.<br /> <br /> I see that the majority of you are professional/academic types. That's interesting. I also see that we have a majority of Ugallu. Also interesting.<br /> <br /> Okay, so, questions for people.<br /> <br /> <b>Samuel Albertine:</b><ul><li>Who is the City Treasurer and why do you think they have an interesting secret?</li> <li>What is the library you work at like?</li> <li>What books are missing from the restricted section?</li> <li>Do you intend on Punishing whoever is taking these books?</li> <li>Can you tell me about a Sin-Eater with whom you have Family Ties?</li> <li>How does your Lair connect with Dorian Long's?</li> <li>What's the most interesting secret you've ever discovered?</li> <li>What's your favorite thing about being a Beast?</li> <li>What do you believe to be true about the Underworld?</li> <li>Are you scared of death?</li> <li>Have you ever killed someone?</li> <li>What do you normally have for breakfast?</li> </ul><b>Elias Carlton:</b><ul><li>Tell me about this hunter cell you lead. Who are its members?</li> <li>How did you end up heading a cancer cell anyway?</li> <li>Who's the mage regenerating your eye? What sorts of favors do you trade with them? Do they have the Family Ties Condition with you?</li> <li>You seem to have a bunch of connections to the supernatural community in Chicago. Who is the city's Apex?</li> <li>What do you think of the Lucifuge hunters?</li> <li>What's the weirdest job your cell has ever done?</li> <li>Which eye is the wounded/regenerated one?</li> <li>What color are your eyes?</li> <li>One of your Aspirations is &quot;Acquire Kinship with a Horror.&quot; Do you mean Primordial Dream monster Horror, or Chronicles of Darkness one-off monster Horror?</li> <li>Why do you want to get in with an Agency?</li> <li>Who's someone you keep in touch with from your air force days?</li> <li>Where in Chicago would you only go under duress?</li> </ul><b>Michael Sellers:</b><ul><li>I don't think you mentioned your three Aspirations. What are they?</li> <li>What does your Lair's Heart look like? Is it that vacuum you mentioned?</li> <li>The Field Museum is right next to the Shedd Aquarium. Why do the Begotten tend to stay away from that place?</li> <li>How long has Raf-Tem been awake?</li> <li>How did you start moonlighting at the Crime Lab?</li> <li>Did you find anything interesting in Bolivia?</li> <li>What's the most recent object you stole from the evidence locker.</li> <li>You say you're a social hunter. With whom do you often hunt?</li> <li>Who are your colleagues? Do you get along with them?</li> <li>Where do you live?</li> <li>Whom do you distrust?</li> </ul><b>Dorian Long:</b><ul><li>How'd you get into the occult therapy game?</li> <li>What is the Chicago Freehold like?</li> <li>Why haven't you become an Oathbound member yet?</li> <li>Who are some of your recurring patients?</li> <li>What do you Collect?</li> <li>How do you like to unwind after a busy day of psychotherapy?</li> <li>What's the longest relationship you've been in?</li> <li>Do you have any theories on the Dreaming Chicago?</li> <li>What are your living quarters like?</li> <li>What do you think of Nathaniel Hargrove?</li> <li>What would you do if you met the Dark Mother tonight?</li> </ul><b>Nathaniel Hargrove:</b><ul><li>How do you feel whenever you see someone performing the saw trick?</li> <li>What's the magician scene in Chicago like?</li> <li>Who's a magician you can't stand?</li> <li>Does your magic specialty apply just to smoke-and-mirrors illusions, or does it cover more arcane territory?</li> <li>How did you meet Julie? What is she like?</li> <li>What's something you find interesting about changelings?</li> <li>What does childhood wonder mean to you?</li> <li>Where's your favorite place to go in Chicago?</li> <li>What do you think of the Dark Mother?</li> <li>Are you currently in therapy?</li> <li>What was your all-time favorite Feeding?</li> <li>Do people ever recognize you on the streets as Mordecai the Mysterious?</li> <li>Who's your biggest fan?</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1423,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","user":"espritdecalmar","date":". 06-20-2016, 09:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T19:05:17-07:00","id":918364,"title":"","content":"Whew, making me work for this one<br /> <br /> <b>Samuel Albertine:</b><ul><li>Who is the City Treasurer and why do you think they have an interesting secret?</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"> The Treasurer was speaking at a commencement ceremony at the university. With Mimir's Wisdom I can tell immediately when someone is lying. Every time he spoke about the city's success and finances I could tell that he was lying. I wasn't able to get close enough to press him for more information.</span></span></span></span><ul><li>What is the library you work at like?</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"> The Library at the university is three stories, open in the center. Samuel spends more time in the library than he does in his own office, roosting on the third floor so he could see over the edge. The restricted section is nearby in a gated off area, Samuel has keys as both a professor, a researcher and he donated some of the first editions in that section. </span></span></span></span><ul><li>What books are missing from the restricted section?</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"> Several first editions, largely of literary works. What's making Samuel concerned is not that they're in the restricted section (though that is a problem) but also because there copies that aren't first editions in the normal sections of the library. It's possible whoever it is might need the first editions for a particular reason, or wasn't aware that there were other copies. It just seems suspicious.</span></span></span></span><ul><li>Do you intend on Punishing whoever is taking these books?</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"> It depends on why. If it's an absent minded college student or someone working on the final stretch of a research paper then he'll understand (but pressure them to return what they don't need). If they've hoarded, damaged or (god forbid) sold/destroyed the books then yes, he'll be seeing red. </span></span></span></span><ul><li>Can you tell me about a Sin-Eater with whom you have Family Ties?</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"> I'll redact the family ties, I thought I had to designate it before trying to create a relationship with one. Samuel is currently trying to track one down to have some guidance through the underworld. So far he's been casting himself blind into the underworld looking for Libraries, but it's been,.. unreliable. He was lucky to discover the library he did for his first chamber. His other attempts have ended either unsuccessfully or with narrow escapes. </span></span></span></span><ul><li>How does your Lair connect with Dorian Long's?</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"> Burrow from empty chamber to one of his empty chambers. Pending Arcanist's approval of course. </span></span></span></span><ul><li>What's the most interesting secret you've ever discovered?</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"> The Library Samuel pulled from the underworld had a breadth of information he wasn't familiar with (though as always, the presence of Omen made much of it familiar). The persistence of the dead in the underworld was shocking, as was the discovery that death is nowhere even remotely near the end of the road. However, it was the sections on the Tenemos he found the most intriguing. Not only was public opinion readily visible there, but it could be altered with ideological attacks. Further study is definitely required. </span></span></span></span><ul><li>What's your favorite thing about being a Beast?</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"> There will never be a limit to what can be discovered, explored and studied. Ever. Humanity, it's origin, destination and deepest depths are all laid bare for a Beast. </span></span></span></span><ul><li>What do you believe to be true about the Underworld?</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"> Anything destroyed has a chance to fall into the underworld. The chances of which are increased exponentially based on the emotional weight of the event in question. At the time the Hero invaded Omen's Heart he had a fair number of followers with him. His death, the death of many others and the burning of the library should have created a significant enough emotional resonance to dump it as a realm in the underworld. Samuel is looking for the lost Library, to recover his lost knowledge. <br /> <br /> If he can't then he'll find copies in other libraries or novel information lost from other places. In truth the persistence of the living dead is a near infinite source of information. Samuel wishes to spend a great deal more time there, but without a guide there are functional problems. </span></span></span></span><ul><li>Are you scared of death?</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"> Not really, Omen will remember Samuel if he dies and he knows that. In a way that's all the immortality he needs. What he's more afraid of is loss, the loss of knowledge that can never be recovered. Samuel can only tap so much of Omen's knowledge in his lifetime but finding physical copies of the books is a different matter. </span></span></span></span><ul><li>Have you ever killed someone?</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"> Samuel, no, Omen, yes. Samuel loathes all things physical, but he wouldn't hesitate to electrocute someone or blow them out the window with Storm Ravaged if he needed to. He doesn't have a lot of attachment to human life as valuable, largely it's that no one has given him enough of a reason to put the effort in as of yet. If he was in a situation where it would be advantageous to kill someone with physical means, he probably wouldn't. Too brutish.</span></span></span></span><ul><li>What do you normally have for breakfast?</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"> Samuel is English on his mothers side so he's inherited some of their mannerisms. Breakfast is normally an eggy in a basket (egg on toast) and a cup of english breakfast tea. Two if it's been a long night. </span></span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10415-vermillionde","name":"VermillionDe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T19:29:51-07:00","id":918374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VermillionDe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/912922-recruitment-city-of-fear?p=918364#post918364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ul><li>How does your Lair connect with Dorian Long's?</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"> Burrow from empty chamber to one of his empty chambers. Pending Arcanist's approval of course. </span></span></span></span>[LIST]</div> </div> </div> </div>Granted. Your second Chamber probably attaches to my second Chamber, so people can swing from your sepulcheral Lair into a replica of the Hedge- yay.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T19:32:10-07:00","id":918375,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4152\" data-vbnamecard=\"4152\">Arcanist</a> That's probably disorienting :P It's good to know that our entire joint lair is one gigantic maze of one kind or another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10415-vermillionde","name":"VermillionDe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T19:45:43-07:00","id":918384,"title":"","content":"The majority of you also have the Maze Lair Trait.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T19:58:21-07:00","id":918389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/912922-recruitment-city-of-fear?p=918346#post918346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[/LIST]<b>Dorian Long:</b><ul><li>How'd you get into the occult therapy game?</li> <li>What is the Chicago Freehold like?</li> <li>Why haven't you become an Oathbound member yet?</li> <li>Who are some of your recurring patients?</li> <li>What do you Collect?</li> <li>How do you like to unwind after a busy day of psychotherapy?</li> <li>What's the longest relationship you've been in?</li> <li>Do you have any theories on the Dreaming Chicago?</li> <li>What are your living quarters like?</li> <li>What do you think of Nathaniel Hargrove?</li> <li>What would you do if you met the Dark Mother tonight?</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Alright, so, in order:<br /> <br /> Dorian has Eyes of Heaven as one of his first Atavisms; seeing people's weaknesses, mundane or otherwise, comes naturally to him. Little things like Vices make perfect sense to him, but when details like &quot;Cold Iron&quot; or &quot;Unable to tell a lie&quot; come up, that's going to make him think twice. The natural senses of the Begotten that allow them to detect Kin paired with his exceptionally keen eyes as an Ugallu and a dragon enabled him to figure out that a not-inconsiderable proportion of his existing clients were waking up screaming from nightmares that he had absolutely nothing to do with. He has a couple other odd customers, but he gravitated towards Changelings because of their natural inclination towards dreams, and also because of his own specialty in treating trauma. From there, things spread by word of mouth, as he started specializing in serving as a safe place to talk about the kinds of things that would get you committed if you told them to another psychiatrist, jumpstarting the healing process in a way conventional therapy wouldn't. His honesty, willingness to reveal his true self, and rigid adherence to the ethical standards of a practicing therapist make him a trustworthy figure in the eyes of the Lost.<br /> <br /> The Chicago Freehold is (because I'm unimaginative right now and would rather not dictate a massive part of the setting) a Seasonal Court (unless you say otherwise). Dreaming Chicago bleeds into the Skein and the Hedge as well, and the Changelings find it rather bothersome. Hobgoblins and more vile fae creatures find plenty of shelter in the structures in the Hedge, and many a cursed bauble emerges from dream Bastions to litter the Hedge. In some groves where Bastions are established the ground is littered with the refuse of torturous dreams. The intense nightmares make it hard to harvest Glamour from dreams, forcing the Freehold to turn to more exploitative means of harvesting it, though they'd rather not. The Autumn Court is highly accepting of Dr. Thorn and what he is, but there is a sizeable (quiet) undercurrent that can't help but notice the similarities between Beast and Gentry. They still come to him, though. He's the best gig in town. Autumn in particular is powerful here because of Dreaming Chicago, and the rest of the Freehold trusts their knowledge. Winter calls for caution and is constantly on high alert, while Summer is intent on patrolling the Hedge and Dreaming Chicago diligently- trying to root out whatever grows there. Spring enjoys the idea of Dreaming Chicago, as it enables them to establish long-standing, expansive Hollows that verge on becoming Hedge Towns. They even have Changeling-specific nightclubs in these Hollows that are built around places where Bastions clump together, enabling groups of Lost to party, gather as much Glamour as they can stomach, and really cut loose. The rest of the Freehold quietly whispers that the rulership of Spring is infested with Loyalists.<br /> <br /> Dorian, though he really wants to be a part of the Freehold, distances himself because <i>so many </i>members of the relatively small, tight-knit community come to him for treatment, and the code of ethics prevents him from establishing multiple relationships with patients to avoid jepordizing their healing process. That, and he strongly suspects the existence of the pervasive element of the Freehold that hates and fears him for what he is. That hurts, but he can at least understand. He fears his own Horror and its tastes sometimes.<br /> <br /> This one I haven't thought much about, but I imagine several high-ranking members of the Courts discreetly come to him. This is another reason he, for now, avoids becoming an Oathbound member of the Freehold- accusations that he is abusing his position of authority to puppeteer the leadership. Dorian, of course, never would, but he would need to wait at least two years after finishing his treatment before considering entering their lives in a different capacity, and he likely won't finish anytime soon. The Changelings are too good a source of food. Perhaps in a few years he'll move on to Mages.<br /> <br /> The Horror would <i>like </i>him to collect mementos of kills, people brought down by their own weaknesses. Dorian himself has determined that all he really needs to subsist off is the shock of having all your weaknesses exposed, and specifically an admission of weakness. He can <i>take </i>the information, but he isn't an Anakim- that doesn't do it for him. He's an Ugallu, he needs his patients to admit that they've been caught and to admit to their own weaknesses. Dorian has absolutely no problem with this, as admission of a problem or a flaw can be cathartic, and it allows for a healthier healing process. This almost certainly triggers Clarity Breaking Points in his patients, but with Dorian's genuine psychiatric treatment and his social finesse in setting up the admission, he hasn't had a patient deteriorate on him, yet. Most come leave with higher Clarity than they did when they came in. To be perfectly clear- he collects admissions of weakness and specifically feeds off of the moment when someone realizes they have been found out and a secret taken from them; they have no choice but to come clean.<br /> <br /> Dorian unwinds from therapy by indulging his own hobbies, reading obsessively on the occult and trying to track down ancient legends of the Begotten and possibly trace the Dark Mother throughout the millennia. He tinkers with theories that will likely never see the light of day outside the Leaden Mirror, Samuel's Lair, or a Mysterium Athanaeum, but he intends to write and publish comprehensive papers on the true nature of dreams, the mind, and the soul- even if his only readers will be a privileged, weird, few.<br /> <br /> Dorian hasn't really been in any kind of extended romantic relationship, or any seriously close friendships. The altered psychology of the Begotten and the Eyes of Heaven make it hard to connect with his human friends and family. He still sees a couple patients from before his Devouring, some he's seen for over six years, but humans don't see their own massive traumas and changes quite as well as a Changeling might. He wants to connect, he really does, but his nature and his training persuades him to isolate. Samuel is probably his closest friend and he's more a colleague than anything.<br /> <br /> Dreaming Chicago is what happens when a city becomes a massive part of someone's identity and even becomes an important character in local folklore. It's Temenos Realm is so close to the Skein that it bleeds through, and even taints the Hedge. He imagines something similar is in place in cities like Detroit or New York.<br /> <br /> Dorian lives in a relatively cozy, but small, apartment near the university. It's sparsely furnished and clean in a way only a space that hasn't been lived in can be, with one obvious area of omission. He has turned the small living room into a virtual library, crammed with bookshelves filled to the brim with psychology books, occult texts, and works in mythology and folklore. He especially loves Jung and Campbell, but for very different reasons. Something that might be easier to miss is a little shrine tucked beside his bed, something oddly primal and crude for the apartment of an erudite intellectual. He actually spends a lot of time in his Lair, meditating by walking the Chambers like a Labyrinth and contemplating the much larger shrine to the Dark Mother within the Heart. He occasionally goes to bother Samuel, though only if he's stuck with a problem- Dorian of all people understands the importance of boundaries.<br /> <br /> Dorian is certain that Nathaniel hasn't, and likely never will, get over his original traumas. He ended treatment because he believes that continuing wouldn't help, but Dorian is at least relieved that he was able to help Nathaniel come to terms with the reality of his situation. He admires Nathaniel's dedication to teaching Lessons, but is worried that he isn't establishing enough of a boundary between himself and his Horror and that it isn't healthy for him to think of the Horror as his deceased rabbit.<br /> <br /> If he met the Dark Mother? Likely fight the urge to abandon his mortal life entirely and learn at her feet. He binds himself to mankind with the rigidity of his ethical code, but the young dragon in his soul yearns to see Mother again. During his Devouring he felt her presence, somewhere far off, a Horror to a Horror, loving and accepting and grim and terrible. He can only describe it as a religious experience. Dorian wants to know the truth, and she's one of the few beings in existence that likely has answers. She's the one that broke him down and revealed his hubris, but she accepted him anyways and adopted him as her own child. That must count for something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 06-20-2016, 11:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T22:29:15-07:00","id":918447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/912922-recruitment-city-of-fear?p=918346#post918346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Michael Sellers:</b><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>I don't think you mentioned your three Aspirations. What are they?</li> <li>What does your Lair's Heart look like? Is it that vacuum you mentioned?</li> <li>The Field Museum is right next to the Shedd Aquarium. Why do the Begotten tend to stay away from that place?</li> <li>How long has Raf-Tem been awake?</li> <li>How did you start moonlighting at the Crime Lab?</li> <li>Did you find anything interesting in Bolivia?</li> <li>What's the most recent object you stole from the evidence locker.</li> <li>You say you're a social hunter. With whom do you often hunt?</li> <li>Who are your colleagues? Do you get along with them?</li> <li>Where do you live?</li> <li>Whom do you distrust?</li> </ol></div> </div> </div> </div><ol class=\"decimal\"><li><ol class=\"lower-alpha\"><li>Find the perfect lynchpin for my collection.</li> <li>Become the senior Collections Manager at Field.</li> <li>Become a better Collector</li> </ol></li> <li>A field of debris floating in the void, so yes.</li> <li>There\u2019s a monster there that suffers no company, accepts no trespass, and holds no quarter or parley. It sleeps fitfully, but hasn\u2019t stirred, yet its presence can be felt around the Granddad exhibit.</li> <li>6 months</li> <li>My character\u2019s field is primarily Forensic Engineering, so they called him in during a rash of \u201cindustrial accidents\u201d where the only commonalities were the victims and the nature of the failures (sabotaged mezzanine supports, yeesh).</li> <li>Some Pre-Columbian petroglyphs that defied easy cataloging and subsequently went missing</li> <li>a scorched bottle of Bacardi 151</li> <li>a couple of older Begotten that showed me the ropes. One\u2019s a dragon. The other\u2019s something stranger.</li> <li>Fitz and Rogers in our Egyptology Department. We are professional.</li> <li>I don\u2019t trust Raf-Tem\u2019s minions, the way that they fawn over him and like to carelessly rifle through things. No respect for process at all.</li> </ol>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T02:01:24-07:00","id":918507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/912922-recruitment-city-of-fear?p=918389#post918389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dorian is certain that Nathaniel hasn't, and likely never will, get over his original traumas. He ended treatment because he believes that continuing wouldn't help, but Dorian is at least relieved that he was able to help Nathaniel come to terms with the reality of his situation. He admires Nathaniel's dedication to teaching Lessons, but is worried that he isn't establishing enough of a boundary between himself and his Horror and that it isn't healthy for him to think of the Horror as his deceased rabbit.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I meant to address this in the backstory, but I neglected to do so, and I apologize for that. I'm going address it now. Hargrove did eventually get over his belief that Warren the Horror was the ghost of Warren the Rabbit, first by believing it to be the symbolic shape that his guilt took in his dreams (thanks to childhood therapy), and eventually as an entity in its own right. He continues to call it Warren, though, because of the fact that he'd been doing so since he was a child and he didn't feel the need to change it after so many years. That said, Hargrove not establishing enough of a boundary between himself and his Horror is a totally fair assessment, and something that he himself worries about. Now to go take care of my own questions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T09:41:18-07:00","id":918668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/912922-recruitment-city-of-fear?p=918389#post918389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Samuel is probably his closest friend and he's more a colleague than anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I don't really see Samuel as the warm and fuzzy type. Not that he has a problem with the company of intelligent people in the slightest, but I could definitely see him not really fulfilling the whole &quot;companionship&quot; need. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10415-vermillionde","name":"VermillionDe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T10:43:43-07:00","id":918691,"title":"","content":"Hoo boy. This is some interesting backstory, and interesting mental health issues on Nathaniel's part.<br /> And those are some peculiar questions. As they say: Never give the Storyteller Ideas. Well screw this, I'm gonna do it either way!<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><ul><li>Q: Tell me about this hunter cell you lead. Who are its members? A: The cell, at the moment consists of Elias and 5 other members. 2 of them are on the Cheiron Group payroll, other 3 are Union. The Cell originally formed as a pure Union one, but two of their members were later offered job at Cheiron and accepted. The Cheiron employees, equipped with any taumatech you see fit, are: Jorge Dispes, a retired (By the ways of getting too close to going Dirty Harry) cop with experience dealing with organized crime, mainly drug cartels, who got into the Vigil after his last case ended in his partner's death by a Claimed junkie, and Nicholas Lodderberg, sport archer formerly with a passion for mundane hunting, who got into the Vigil after barely escaping alive from a Werewolf Pack whose territory he entered when hunting. The Union Members are: Colette Lynx, a high-school Design &amp; Technology teacher who took up the Vigil after her sister started attending a vampire night club and subsequently became one of the Kindred's walking blood bank and slave (the vampire in question later got &quot;visited&quot; by a very pissed Elias and carefully explained why doing such things is bad for you), Ronald Werrety, an IT geek, freelance programmer and ridiculously skilled hacker whose candle was lit after he found out that the stuff that caused his dad to go bankrupt and ultimately broke his family wasn't exactly 100% human, and last but not least, George Vincent, MD, a surgeon who had waaay too many cases of supernatural injuries at his operating table not to start wondering. The cell's main base of operations and territory is Pill Hill, but they do stuff all over the city.</li> <li>Q:How did you end up heading a cancer cell anyway? A: The situation was actually pretty simple. He lives in the same neighborhood as the rest of the cell, and it's not that secret that he is a former military. Which means that when the Cell needed someone with experience similiar to his, to help with the &quot;Demonic Possession&quot; problem a few years back, they came to him. And he, seeing an opportunity for having some fun while also possibly dealing some collateral damage to sate the <s>Douchelizard</s> Wyvern, accepted. After the matter has been dealt with, he told them to contact him if they're ever doing something like that again. Well, the point of organized monster hunting is to do such things more often, and so after a few such situations, he was officially accepted into the cell. It has quickly turned out that Elias was the most knowledgable and somehow experienced of them all in maters supernatural. He handwaved this by a &quot;There were supernaturals in Iraq too&quot;. Either way, due to this, gradually, over time, while not becoming a leader per se, he got to be the one calling the shots, largely thanks to his &quot;Govs&quot; contacts.</li> <li>Who's the mage regenerating your eye? What sorts of favors do you trade with them? Do they have the Family Ties Condition with you? A: The mage in question introduces himself as Tiberius. He's a Thyrsus of the Silver Ladder, and the Provost to the Magistos Councilor. Utterly amoral (but not unwise) thinking about everything in terms of buisness and the gain/lose bilance, ruthless and efficient buisnessman involved in the cities drug trade. The trade of favours between Elias and Tiberius is fairly simple: Tiberius regularily regenerates Elias' eye(He knew better than to make it permament and no other Adept/Master of Life in the City would do it), and ocassionaly impersonates a Barret Comission official before the Cell. In exchange, if Tiberius ever has a task to be dealt with, some drugs to be delivered, someone to be silenced, some powerful artifact to be stolen, anything really, Elias does it for him, for free(Not counting the eye and the impersonation, but those are trivial, really). They do not have established Family Ties. Their relationship is strictly buisness.</li> <li>You seem to have a bunch of connections to the supernatural community in Chicago. Who is the city's Apex? Elias does not yet know for sure. About half a year ago there was an apparent change in the position of the Apex (Previous Apex was the current Adamantine Sage, known for the fiery temper and liberal usage of fireballs). All signs on the Earth and Primordial Dream seem to point at a werewolf calling himself &quot;The Ripper Claw&quot;, or, as he's being called by some younger ones when they're absolutely sure he's at least two dozen city blocks away and in another plane of reality &quot;Doomguy&quot;. Alpha of the city's largest Predator Kings pack. A sadistic, cruel, ruthless and pretty much batshit insane murderer, as well as one of the most powerful amongst the Pure, who revels in the bloodbath he lays in his wake regularily. It's either him who's the Apex, or somehow the position of the Apex has been taken by a Hero, and no Beast in the city doesn't want to even think of this being a possibility.</li> <li><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Q: What do you think of the Lucifuge hunters? A: Elias genuinely likes them. They're good kids, really, and while not necessarily subscribing to their beliefs, he thinks of them as being rather admirable in their persistence. It's just that they have deeper relations with the Supernatural community than all other hunters maybe except for The Ascending Ones, and can actually see the pattern going on with Elias' cell.</span></li> <li>Q: What's the weirdest job your cell has ever done? A: Alright, so you know what Plica Polonica is? Yeah. It's a thing that practically never happens in the modern world, outside of dreadlocks and third world countries. So imagine the surprise of many a-human(Who, by the way, do indeed practice proper hair care), when they wake up one day, and it's starting to form there, on their heads. And indeed, in a few days, it was spreading like a plague over the less metropolized parts of the city, not reaching further north than Avalon Park, at least to everyone that is still pretty much mortal (So Wolves don't get it, Changelings don't get it, but Mages verily so). George and his peers are working on something that'd fit better in 19th century rural areas of Poland, not in a metropolis like the goddamned Chicago, mainly an anti-trichoma campaign, but trying to use the experience from back then didn't really work. What's more, the gathered plaits are disappearing before they can be get rid of, and George began a little investigation on his own, also dragging the rest of the cell into it. Beacause those plaits clearly had something supernatural to them. Unseen Sense, ya'know? Either way, they decicded to do this by the simplest of means: Stay at where the cut down trichomas are being kept, and see what happens to them. Imagine their complete lack of surprise when the hair started to move on its own in a somehow organized fashion. Well, do they stop the hair right there? Nope, they follow it to where's it going. So they follow a couple stacks of crawling hair, all the way to Altgeld Gardens. And then it sorta, disappears. I mean, they loose track of it. So they decide to search, It couldn't just poof out of existance, like that, right? Fortunately they don't split up, and after some looking around they find what the plaits were going for. A giant monster made out entirely of plaits, consisting of a vaguely humanoid upper half and octopus-like lower half with trichoma tentacles. Which promptly proceded to beat the crap out of all six of them. Elias lasted the longest, mainly by staying out of reach, and when everybody else got knocked out and he was barely in a better condition, he decided to fire of a couple Satiety-powered Dragonfires, which seemed to do better against the thing than conventional means of applying damage, but barely. Before he got to do some more of the good stuff, however, he also got knocked out, and when all of the cell woke up, the monstrosity was not there anymore. Also, the problem with plaits has ended, so that's a good thing, right?</li> <li>Q: Which eye is the wounded/regenerated one? A: Right</li> <li>Q: What color are your eyes? A: A shade of yellowish brown.</li> <li>Q: One of your Aspirations is &quot;Acquire Kinship with a Horror.&quot; Do you mean Primordial Dream monster Horror, or Chronicles of Darkness one-off monster Horror? A: The Dread-Powered one-off monster kind, yes. The freaky accident described above is actually what pushed him to this aspiration.</li> <li>Q: Why do you want to get in with an Agency? A: It's largely a matter of ambition. Every large organized group in the city hired him at least once. The Pure, the Forsaken, the Pentacle Consilium, the Seer Ministries, the Invictus, the Lancea et Sanctum, hell, even the Freehold had a job for him once. But not any of the Agencies with Chicago as their base of operations. Not even once. That, and he kinda' considers the whole Demon/Beast antagonism a fuckton of bullshit. Okay, cool, they're not family. That one dude next door isn't family too, but do you have a Shiites/Sunnis relationship going on with him? He wants to improve the relationship between the two splats, and he feels that establishing buisness with the Unchained bigwigs will help it greatly.</li> <li>Q: Who's someone you keep in touch with from your air force days? A: Marcy <span style=\"font-family:arial\">Vand\u00edc\u00e9, a mechanic who served at the base Elias stationed in back in Iraq. A small-ish girl of vaguely asian looks, always cheerful, smiling, upbeat, shining beacon of joy and optimism wherever she goes and seemingly immune to everything even remotely negative. She hasn't stopped working for the military and currently serves at the Scott Air Force Base.</span></li> <li>Where in Chicago would you only go under duress? A: Norwood Park. Territorry of the aformentioned Predator Kings pack.</li> </ul></div></div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1423_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1423\" data-vbnamecard=\"1423\">espritdecalmar</a> If you'd like an extended writeup on any of the characters here, be it Jorge, Colette, George, Tiberius, Doomguy, Marcy or anyone else, just say and I'll PM you","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11117,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","user":"Inquisitor","date":". 06-22-2016, 12:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","name":"Inquisitor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T11:07:27-07:00","id":918703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Inquisitor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/912922-recruitment-city-of-fear?p=918691#post918691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hoo boy. This is some interesting backstory, and interesting mental health issues on Nathaniel's part.<br /> And those are some peculiar questions. As they say: Never give the Storyteller Ideas. Well screw this, I'm gonna do it either way!<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><ul><li>Q: Tell me about this hunter cell you lead. Who are its members? A: The cell, at the moment consists of Elias and 5 other members. 2 of them are on the Cheiron Group payroll, other 3 are Union. The Cell originally formed as a pure Union one, but two of their members were later offered job at Cheiron and accepted. The Cheiron employees, equipped with any taumatech you see fit, are: Jorge Dispes, a retired (By the ways of getting too close to going Dirty Harry) cop with experience dealing with organized crime, mainly drug cartels, who got into the Vigil after his last case ended in his partner's death by a Claimed junkie, and Nicholas Lodderberg, sport archer formerly with a passion for mundane hunting, who got into the Vigil after barely escaping alive from a Werewolf Pack whose territory he entered when hunting. The Union Members are: Colette Lynx, a high-school Design &amp; Technology teacher who took up the Vigil after her sister started attending a vampire night club and subsequently became one of the Kindred's walking blood bank and slave (the vampire in question later got &quot;visited&quot; by a very pissed Elias and carefully explained why doing such things is bad for you), Ronald Werrety, an IT geek, freelance programmer and ridiculously skilled hacker whose candle was lit after he found out that the stuff that caused his dad to go bankrupt and ultimately broke his family wasn't exactly 100% human, and last but not least, George Vincent, MD, a surgeon who had waaay too many cases of supernatural injuries at his operating table not to start wondering. The cell's main base of operations and territory is Pill Hill, but they do stuff all over the city.</li> <li>Q:How did you end up heading a cancer cell anyway? A: The situation was actually pretty simple. He lives in the same neighborhood as the rest of the cell, and it's not that secret that he is a former military. Which means that when the Cell needed someone with experience similiar to his, to help with the &quot;Demonic Possession&quot; problem a few years back, they came to him. And he, seeing an opportunity for having some fun while also possibly dealing some collateral damage to sate the <s>Douchelizard</s> Wyvern, accepted. After the matter has been dealt with, he told them to contact him if they're ever doing something like that again. Well, the point of organized monster hunting is to do such things more often, and so after a few such situations, he was officially accepted into the cell. It has quickly turned out that Elias was the most knowledgable and somehow experienced of them all in maters supernatural. He handwaved this by a &quot;There were supernaturals in Iraq too&quot;. Either way, due to this, gradually, over time, while not becoming a leader per se, he got to be the one calling the shots, largely thanks to his &quot;Govs&quot; contacts.</li> <li>Who's the mage regenerating your eye? What sorts of favors do you trade with them? Do they have the Family Ties Condition with you? A: The mage in question introduces himself as Tiberius. He's a Thyrsus of the Silver Ladder, and the Provost to the Magistos Councilor. Utterly amoral (but not unwise) thinking about everything in terms of buisness and the gain/lose bilance, ruthless and efficient buisnessman involved in the cities drug trade. The trade of favours between Elias and Tiberius is fairly simple: Tiberius regularily regenerates Elias' eye(He knew better than to make it permament and no other Adept/Master of Life in the City would do it), and ocassionaly impersonates a Barret Comission official before the Cell. In exchange, if Tiberius ever has a task to be dealt with, some drugs to be delivered, someone to be silenced, some powerful artifact to be stolen, anything really, Elias does it for him, for free(Not counting the eye and the impersonation, but those are trivial, really). They do not have established Family Ties. Their relationship is strictly buisness.</li> <li>You seem to have a bunch of connections to the supernatural community in Chicago. Who is the city's Apex? Elias does not yet know for sure. About half a year ago there was an apparent change in the position of the Apex (Previous Apex was the current Adamantine Sage, known for the fiery temper and liberal usage of fireballs). All signs on the Earth and Primordial Dream seem to point at a werewolf calling himself &quot;The Ripper Claw&quot;, or, as he's being called by some younger ones when they're absolutely sure he's at least two dozen city blocks away and in another plane of reality &quot;Doomguy&quot;. Alpha of the city's largest Predator Kings pack. A sadistic, cruel, ruthless and pretty much batshit insane murderer, as well as one of the most powerful amongst the Pure, who revels in the bloodbath he lays in his wake regularily. It's either him who's the Apex, or somehow the position of the Apex has been taken by a Hero, and no Beast in the city doesn't want to even think of this being a possibility.</li> <li><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Q: What do you think of the Lucifuge hunters? A: Elias genuinely likes them. They're good kids, really, and while not necessarily subscribing to their beliefs, he thinks of them as being rather admirable in their persistence. It's just that they have deeper relations with the Supernatural community than all other hunters maybe except for The Ascending Ones, and can actually see the pattern going on with Elias' cell.</span></li> <li>Q: What's the weirdest job your cell has ever done? A: [It's gona be a pretty lenghty answer and I already spent way too much time on this so expect it tomorrow]</li> <li>Q: Which eye is the wounded/regenerated one? A: Right</li> <li>Q: What color are your eyes? A: A shade of yellowish brown.</li> <li>Q: One of your Aspirations is &quot;Acquire Kinship with a Horror.&quot; Do you mean Primordial Dream monster Horror, or Chronicles of Darkness one-off monster Horror? A: The Dread-Powered one-off monster kind, yes. The freaky accident described above is actually what pushed him to this aspiration.</li> <li>Q: Why do you want to get in with an Agency? A: It's largely a matter of ambition. Every large organized group in the city hired him at least once. The Pure, the Forsaken, the Pentacle Consilium, the Seer Ministries, the Invictus, the Lancea et Sanctum, hell, even the Freehold had a job for him once. But not any of the Agencies with Chicago as their base of operations. Not even once. That, and he kinda' considers the whole Demon/Beast antagonism a fuckton of bullshit. Okay, cool, they're not family. That one dude next door isn't family too, but do you have a Shiites/Sunnis relationship going on with him? He wants to improve the relationship between the two splats, and he feels that establishing buisness with the Unchained bigwigs will help it greatly.</li> <li>Q: Who's someone you keep in touch with from your air force days? A: Marcy <span style=\"font-family:arial\">Vand\u00edc\u00e9, a mechanic who served at the base Elias stationed in back in Iraq. A small-ish girl of vaguely asian looks, always cheerful, smiling, upbeat, shining beacon of joy and optimism wherever she goes and seemingly immune to everything even remotely negative. She hasn't stopped working for the military and currently serves at the Scott Air Force Base.</span></li> <li>Where in Chicago would you only go under duress? A: Norwood Park. Territorry of the aformentioned Predator Kings pack.</li> </ul></div></div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1423_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1423\" data-vbnamecard=\"1423\">espritdecalmar</a> If you'd like an extended writeup on any of the characters here, be it Jorge, Colette, George, Tiberius, Doomguy, Marcy or anyone else, just say and I'll PM you</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeesh. And I thought the plot hooks I was suggesting would lead to trouble<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T12:20:40-07:00","id":918740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/912922-recruitment-city-of-fear?p=918703#post918703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeesh. And I thought the plot hooks I was suggesting would lead to trouble<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>When it comes to kneecapping yourself to the storyteller, my attitude is Go Big or Go Home.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","name":"Inquisitor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T08:59:15-07:00","id":919121,"title":"","content":"Hmm, I'm thinking I want to make a couple of tweaks to my character. For one, I ALWAYS confused You Are Alone and You Are Not Alone (the latter of which I meant to take). But I'm really struggling on my Beasts hunger. Just about everything in my background is pointing to the idea that he should be a collector, looking for his lost books. However he'd still be pretty angry about what happened to his, not to mention angry at anyone who tries to fabricate and lie about the truth. I think playing a Nemesis would be more fun, but I also can't help but see how being a collector may make more sense in the long run. What do you guys think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10415-vermillionde","name":"VermillionDe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T09:28:37-07:00","id":919134,"title":"","content":"I vote Nemesis, just going on your backstory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T10:05:33-07:00","id":919160,"title":"","content":"I vote Collector, since judging by the question answers, he really doesn't seem to be too Nemesis-y.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","name":"Inquisitor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T06:20:56-07:00","id":919670,"title":"","content":"Well I re-read collector in the book and it's making me hesitate. I guess one of the aspects with collector is that in order for it to count for feeding someone has to feel a loss for what you took. As in, if I found a book that I wanted someone would have to be upset that I took it. I don't think my character is really concerned about that in the least, he just wants his books back. In fact, I think he'd be more inclined to take a book from a person who DIDN'T appreciate it than one who did. One of the inspirations for the character is the fear of inadequacy, like the impostor effect (where you question whether you deserve the success that you have regardless of how much evidence there is). Rather than make that what he played on I wanted to have him punish the ACTUAL impostors (you know, the ones who ironically don't suffer from the impostor effect). Hmm, I guess in a way what I really wanted to punish was stupidity but this seemed to be the best way to do that that was still in keeping with the character. <br /> <br /> Ok, I'm going to stay as a nemesis because I don't think collector makes as much sense. I'd love to have Nemesis for stupidity but I'm not sure how I'd go about that one, it may be ill defined. The impostor idea plays well into being an Ugallu (that way I get to expose them) which also works with cheating, I suppose. I'm not sure stupidity falls into that category quite as well as I'd like. Hmm, I'll stay with what I'm doing for now but I may want to look at what my focus for nemesis is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10415-vermillionde","name":"VermillionDe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T08:06:02-07:00","id":919715,"title":"","content":"You could always make it the punishment of willful ignorance, punishing those that could know better and deliberately choose against knowledge. That would still leave cheaters as valid targets, as they have chosen to cheat instead of learning the material. It would mean that he wasn't punishing people for not having much intelligence naturally, but there's no shortage of people out there that just don't want to think.<br /> <br /> As far as the Collectors go, I'm not sure that the object being missed is quite as important as the book seems to indicate, as Collectors are also mentioned as collecting lovers or ancient forgotten treasures. It seems like they need to either take something from someone else or earn it through great personal effort for it to count.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T08:59:49-07:00","id":919745,"title":"","content":"Hmm, punishing willful ignorance is probably the best description. He wouldn't be angry at someone who just isn't very bright (he'd probably feel bad for them) but rather be angry at someone who absolutely could understand something but chose not to. So yeah, shortcuts like cheating, pretending to know something or willfully keeping oneself ignorant would probably make him want to tear his hair out. ... or molt. <br /> <br /> Hmm, yeah I don't see him really enjoying as much of the effort of trying to collect something. It's not about the effort or earning it, it's about protecting it from negligence and storing it for when its needed. So collector maybe not the best fit, if there was a curator type perhaps... :P <br /> <br /> Thanks <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar309_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"309\" data-vbnamecard=\"309\">White Oak Dragon</a>, I think you definitely gave me a few things to think about in regards to Nemesis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10415-vermillionde","name":"VermillionDe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T09:06:43-07:00","id":919749,"title":"","content":"Perhaps he simply punishes them by taking that which they don't use as they should. Like fines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T12:52:10-07:00","id":919879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/912922-recruitment-city-of-fear?p=919749#post919749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps he simply punishes them by taking that which they don't use as they should. Like fines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you mean in the capacity of a collector? Because in this characters case he wants *his* books back, the ones that were lost when a Hero burned down half his Heart chamber. If he saw one of his books it wouldn't matter if it was in the library of some rich superstar who never set foot in the same room, on display at the Smithsonian, in the care of someone who loved it intensely or being sold for 2.99 at a second hand bookstore. ...he'd probably care *a little* if someone loved the book intensely, but that might be because he'd sympathize with their loss. <br /> <br /> Wow, it occurs to me that I'd love to make a nightmare that would punish stupid people. &quot;You got this&quot;: Instills a fear that they don't really know what they're doing, but they can't let anyone know that so they just keep pretending regardless of what anyone tells them. Though that might be too functionally similar to &quot;Everything you do is worthless&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10415-vermillionde","name":"VermillionDe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T13:02:50-07:00","id":919885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VermillionDe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/912922-recruitment-city-of-fear?p=919879#post919879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you mean in the capacity of a collector? Because in this characters case he wants *his* books back, the ones that were lost when a Hero burned down half his Heart chamber. If he saw one of his books it wouldn't matter if it was in the library of some rich superstar who never set foot in the same room, on display at the Smithsonian, in the care of someone who loved it intensely or being sold for 2.99 at a second hand bookstore. ...he'd probably care *a little* if someone loved the book intensely, but that might be because he'd sympathize with their loss. <br /> <br /> Wow, it occurs to me that I'd love to make a nightmare that would punish stupid people. &amp;quot;You got this&amp;quot;: Instills a fear that they don't really know what they're doing, but they can't let anyone know that so they just keep pretending regardless of what anyone tells them. Though that might be too functionally similar to &amp;quot;Everything you do is worthless&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean that taking things is his method of Punishment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T13:59:22-07:00","id":919934,"title":"","content":"Ohhhh, I misunderstood. Hmm, possible, and that would make for a great magpie Beast (filing that idea away for later) but I really wanted to hit with the Ugallu concept of Exposure. So the punishment in this idea comes from exposing the lies, cheating and false practices. That part of the concept I'm pretty happy with. That's a good idea though, almost like a Beast kindergarten teacher who takes away your ball when you do bad things. Except in this case it may be pulling all your teeth out or something. Kinda reminds me of the Beldan from Coraline. I had always thought of her as a True Fae but now I think Beast might fit better. She has her own realm afterall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10415-vermillionde","name":"VermillionDe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T18:26:38-07:00","id":920055,"title":"","content":"Okay, here's the answers to my questions. I rambled on again, so I'm sharing a link instead of posting them directly to the thread.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_AXRfImh-kVblA2YnZvbWg1TVU/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_AXRfImh-kVblA2YnZvbWg1TVU/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_AXRfImh-kVblA2YnZvbWg1TVU/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_AXRfImh-kVblA2YnZvbWg1TVU/view?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T06:08:32-07:00","id":920312,"title":"","content":"Added to bucket list: Chicago Magic Lounge","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10415-vermillionde","name":"VermillionDe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T08:27:38-07:00","id":920380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VermillionDe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/912922-recruitment-city-of-fear?p=920312#post920312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Added to bucket list: Chicago Magic Lounge</div> </div> </div> </div>I know what you mean. I wish I'd known about it back when I lived up there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T17:02:09-07:00","id":922923,"title":"","content":"Alright, this is all looking great. Really fantastic. I think I have enough to start up a game. I'm going to compile some more notes and find a platform for it. In the meantime, I have one more question/request for each of you: Please tell me about another Beast who lives in Chicago. It can be fairly bare-bones: Family, Hunger, Horror, interesting fact, what you think of them. Just so we can populate our city a bit and give it some character.<br /> <br /> Also, I want to talk a bit about my Storytelling style.<br /> <br /> I'm more into collaboration than antagonism. I figure we're creating this story together, what happens is in your hands as much as mine. I don't know what's going to happen; all I can do is follow the rules of the game and the laws of physics and drama (usually drama) and see what comes of it. I'm also more interested in saying yes than no. Sometimes (oftentimes) that'll turn into a &quot;Yes, and&quot; or &quot;Yes, but&quot; but if you want to throw something in, some interesting tidbit about this world, then so long as it doesn't contradict what's already established, so long as it's cool and interesting, then I say, absolutely go for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T18:41:09-07:00","id":922969,"title":"","content":"Wow, your style of storytelling is very different than mine. I'm pretty strict with my players characters generation but they can achieve or attain next to anything as long as they put the legwork in.<br /> <br /> Name: Harmony Skala<br /> Hunger: Ravager (Ruin Marriages/Families)<br /> Horror: Makara, Siren<br /> Atavisms: Sirens Treacherous Song, Alien Allure, Eye of Heaven<br /> Notable Merits: Striking Looks (Advanced), Contacts(Benefactors)<br /> <br /> Harmony is a social predator of spectacular fashion. Her lineage oozes a mystical appeal that few men (or women) can deny. It takes her little effort to feed as all she needs to do is take a willing man home, snap a few selfies with his phone and text whatever number is asking him to &quot;Pick up (milk/eggs/bread/the kids)&quot;. Then its sit back and watch it all fall apart. Harmony enjoys an easy life at the top, frequently coming across other supernaturals engaging in similar feeding strategies, most often Kindred of the Daeva clan. She can easily milk a meal for more than just Satiety by letting them shower her with gifts before bringing their lives down in ruins around them.<br /> <br /> Harmony met Samuel by way of a fund raising dinner for wealthy benefactors of the university. She was looking for her next target as her current meal was arguing with his wife about why he brought a date. Confusing Samuel for a wealthy benefactor, she was surprised to find that he really couldn't care less about her. Despite multiple advances Professor Albertine still refused to even feign interest. Which he never admitted had a large amount to do with the fact that he was fairly certain a patron at his table owned one of his books. Additionally, being an all knowing asexual Owl monster was something of a factor.<br /> <br /> Samuel and Harmony keep in visceral touch as fellow Beasts. They stay in entirely different circles and can find each other a good barometer for what's happening in the city at large. Harmony appreciates Samuel's opinion as he's probably one of the only men who's end game isn't in her pants. Samuel appreciates Harmony's insights as someone who, you know, has feelings and can speak to human beings. The two never made it past fleeting friendly advice as they both hold the same opinion of each other: More than brief contact would be a bit much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10415,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10415-vermillionde","user":"VermillionDe","date":". 06-28-2016, 09:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10415-vermillionde","name":"VermillionDe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T18:58:01-07:00","id":922981,"title":"","content":"You can always use the character ideas I mentioned early if you want. I can try to write them out more, if you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T21:56:59-07:00","id":923070,"title":"","content":"<b>Name: </b>Jemma Kerr<br /> <b>Family:</b> Namtaru<br /> <b>Hunger:</b> Predator (Transgressors)<br /> <b>Horror:</b> Grey Goo (Unbreakable, Infestation, Monster from the Deep, Heart of the Ocean, Basilisk's Touch, All Your Teeth are Falling Out, Bugs Everywhere!, You are Infected)<br /> <b>Interesting Notes: </b>works for the local Nosferatu as security/decoration out in Garfield Park. Former Blood Doll. Jealous of interlopers.<br /> <b>Sellers' Opinion: </b>She can't be trusted. She's overzealous, shameless, and above all, an addict. You don't mess with her unless you have no other choice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":1959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","user":"Hexmeister Vic","date":".  Had to fix the Family, as she's very much focused on being unlikable rather than merely dangerous. 06-29-2016, 08:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T02:19:57-07:00","id":923766,"title":"","content":"Aaalright, give you a Beast NPC to work with, huh? Can do.<br /> <br /> <b>Name: </b>Tobiasz Dwernicki<br /> <b>Family: </b>Anakim<br /> <b>Hunger: </b>Nemesis (Those who wage conflict)<br /> <b>Horror: </b>A gigantic black dog, made out of black smoke, dragging leftovers of brokne iron chains behind him,<br /> <b>Notable Nightmares and Atavisms: </b>From the Shadows, Limb from Limb, Looming Presence, Monster from the Deep, Titanic Blow, Behold, My True Form!, Fear is Contagius, Run Away, You Will Never Rest<br /> <b>Notable Merits: </b>Giant<br /> <b>Backstory: </b>Tobiasz is one of thousands of Polish immigrants in Chicago, who came there in late 90's, following the city's reputation with Beasts. And, immediately following his arrival, he opened a bar in Stanislawowo. But not just any normal bar, you see. This one has an interesting policy. First off, three kinds of people are not allowed in: Mortals, Demons and Politicians. Second off, you misbehave, you're out. Violently. Sometimes the patrons themselves take care of you. Why? Well, Tobiasz commands great respect, that's for one. Even before coming to Chicago he was a powerful Beast in his own right. That, and his bar serves as a rare case of completely and utterly neutral ground, and God Machine/Principle/Dark Mother/Whoever knows that it's something of great value around these parts and few would like to get depraved of something this useful. And those few who wouldn't mind aren't the sort to need it in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","name":"Inquisitor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T19:48:46-07:00","id":924249,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking my way through an NPC- will probably get something out tomorrow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T15:59:57-07:00","id":924661,"title":"","content":"I'm working on mine as well. Hopefully I'll be able to get him done tonight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T18:38:38-07:00","id":924706,"title":"","content":"Sweet deal. I believe in you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T11:24:55-07:00","id":924962,"title":"","content":"Okay, apparently, early this afternoon is the new last night. Enjoy.<br /> <br /> <b>Name:</b> Henry \u201cHank\u201d Richardson<br /> <b>Family:</b> Eshmaki<br /> <b>Hunger:</b> Predator - The Marrow Hound hungers for bone marrow, the fresher the better. The Horror wants nothing more than for Hank to stalk people through the narrow passages of the Wasteland or the alleys of the city, render them helpless and begin cracking open bones with his teeth to feast.<br /> <b>Horror:</b> The Marrow Hound appears as a vicious emaciated wolf. His grayish flesh is wrinkled and hairless, and it is pierced through with jagged shards of bone, giving the creature a spiked appearance.<br /> <b>Lair: </b>(Traits - Jagged, Echoing, Maze) The Wasteland is a confusing network of twisted, steep walled gray canyons, the cliffs towering as high as skyscrapers. The ravines are littered with jagged rocks and the shattered bones of previous victims. Roiling storm clouds race by overhead, with occasional rumbles of thunder echoing, although no rain ever seems to fall.<br /> <b>Legend:</b> Relentless<br /> <b>Life:</b> Hopeful<br /> <b>Atavisms:</b> From The Shadows, Limb From Limb, Unbreakable<br /> <b>Nightmares:</b> Everything You Do Is Worthless, You Are Alone, You Deserve This, Your Rage Consumes You<br /> <b>Backstory:</b> Hank is easily dismissed by most of the people of the city. While he is a very friendly individual, his ragged beard and dusty, tattered clothing immediately marks him as one of the city\u2019s many homeless people. Hank doesn\u2019t let it get him down, though. He still has a smile and a cheerful greeting for everyone who walks by his usual spot, which is not far from Union Station.<br /> Hank was once a school teacher in one of Chicago\u2019s inner city high schools. His cheerful attitude made him surprisingly popular with his students, although some of the parents didn\u2019t appreciate his boundless optimism. One child\u2019s father came to confront him after he had provided his son with pamphlets for various colleges. The parent was enraged, because he felt that Hank had been setting his son up for disappointment by showing him a life that could never be provided. Hank argued that with scholarships, the child could very well become whatever he wished to be, even if it would be a struggle. Unfortunately, Hank had gone through his Devouring not too long before. Horrified by what his Horror desired, he had refused to feed his Hunger at all, and his Satiety had dwindled far too much. This, coupled with the heightened tempers of the moment, led to Hank crunching one of the man\u2019s fingers. This led to a short time in jail, and a nightmarish experience for the other inmates as his Horror raged through their dreamscapes night after night. His cellmate, though, proved different from the other inmates. This one, Mickey, would let himself out of his cell some nights, and beat the living hell out of whichever inmate had pissed him off most recently. Hank discovered that when he witnessed Mickey terrorizing another, he was able to feed his Horror on the same fear that the brute was feeding upon.<br /> Upon his release, he soon determined that few people were willing to employ a person who had been jailed for biting off the finger of another. This quickly led to homelessness, and a new life relying on the kindness of strangers just to survive. He still refused to feed his Horror the marrow it sought, though, and without his cellmate, the Horror\u2019s Hunger began to grow. Realizing that eventually things might get out of hand once more, Hank decided to seek out another ogre to befriend. What he found instead were men that would run as wolves, hunting down man and creature alike. Since then, he has made contact with most of the city\u2019s packs, and established Family Ties with both Pure and Forsaken werewolves. Hank now sees himself as playing a vital role in the city, acting as a self-appointed mediator between the Pure and the Forsaken, and between the various packs of the city and the Begotten. Most of the packs don\u2019t mind him tagging along on their hunts, although the Predator Kings barely tolerate him at the best of times. His Horror delights in hunting alongside the various packs, even if it would prefer Hank to hunt for marrow instead.<br /> Hargrove has met Hank, but doesn\u2019t know him very well. He often gives him handouts of food or change when he sees him, as Hargrove pities the poor man. Hank accepts the handouts, but doesn\u2019t see the need for the pity, as he has grown to enjoy his life, and has every confidence that things will work out for the best.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T02:26:11-07:00","id":925803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VermillionDe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/912922-recruitment-city-of-fear?p=922969#post922969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Harmony is a social predator of spectacular fashion. Her lineage oozes a mystical appeal that few men (or women) can deny. It takes her little effort to feed as all she needs to do is take a willing man home, snap a few selfies with his phone and text whatever number is asking him to &quot;Pick up (milk/eggs/bread/the kids)&quot;. Then its sit back and watch it all fall apart.</div> </div> </div> </div>It occurs to me that if Harmony became especially hungry, she'd have another quick and easy way to feed, too. All she'd need to do is go to a club or a bar and look for a guy finding a quiet corner to call home. When he starts with the &quot;Sorry, Honey, I've got to stay late at work tonight&quot; excuses, she could simply slip up behind him and say, &quot;Honey, hang up the phone and come back to bed,&quot; loudly enough for the person on the other end to hear. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T08:43:25-07:00","id":925919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/912922-recruitment-city-of-fear?p=925803#post925803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> All she'd need to do is go to a club or a bar and look for a guy finding a quiet corner to call home. When he starts with the &quot;Sorry, Honey, I've got to stay late at work tonight&quot; excuses, she could simply slip up behind him and say, &quot;Honey, hang up the phone and come back to bed,&quot; loudly enough for the person on the other end to hear. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh absolutely, even if they heard the music in the background she could always offer a lap dance or shout &quot;Hey! Hands off the dancers!&quot;. For those quick and dirty feedings :P I actually love the concept, I may have to try it next time my group wants to try a beast story that I'm not telling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10415-vermillionde","name":"VermillionDe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T10:07:47-07:00","id":925948,"title":"","content":"These are all looking very good! We'll be starting soon, btw. I just need to put the finishing touches on some things. Incidentally, I'm visiting a Frank Lloyd Wright today, so I'll be returning from a distant land of crystals and bridges with architectural inspiration.<br /> <br /> I think also, by the way, we'll be starting off with a day-in-the-life scenario, to see what you all do in your daily routines (especially since last I checked you're all starting Sated anyway, so no one's in particular need of a midnight snack).<br /> <br /> Also, as a final summary, to make sure we're all on the same page here, these are our actors as I understand them:<ul><li>Samuel Albertine, Ugallu Nemesis: A truth-seeking librarian who stalks the shelves for offenders against forbidden knowledge.</li> <li>Elias Carlton, Ugallu Ravager: A former military pilot who leads a hunter cell with ties to every corner of Chicago's bestiary.</li> <li>Michael Sellers, Makara Collector: A physical anthropologist at the Field Museum with a penchant for stealing from evidence lockers.</li> <li>Dorian Long, Ugallu Collector: A &quot;shrink for the strange&quot; with aspirations to join the Chi-town changeling freehold who teaches patients to acknowledge their weaknesses.</li> <li>Nathaniel Hargrove, aka Mordecai the Mysterious, Eshmaki Tyrant: A stage magician with a long-standing anxiety about saw tricks trying to recover his childhood sense of wonder while struggling to reconcile his Bestial and human natures.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T16:52:46-07:00","id":926163,"title":"","content":"Sam is a professor, but Librarian is a pretty apt description regardless.Otherwise yeah I'm cool with that. Looking forward to starting!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10415-vermillionde","name":"VermillionDe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T10:58:47-07:00","id":927683,"title":"","content":"Yeah, you pretty much nailed it there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","name":"Inquisitor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T15:03:01-07:00","id":927791,"title":"","content":"Mordecai's description seems pretty apt as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i